    {'code': '794003', 'port_slug': 'alicante', 'title': 'Glorious Guadalest', 'slug': 'glorious-guadalest-794003', 'price': 109.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/794003-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTc3NTJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREkzTDJoalpTODVOamMxTmpZNU1UYzJNelV3THpjNU5EQXdNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w2NWJkMDI4ZDAyMDJhMjg5NDVhMDBkOWJkMWI0ZThlODdmZDVjMGVjOTQ2Nzk4YjZiMTIzMWM2ZjFmN2JmODc3', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '794012', 'port_slug': 'alicante', 'title': 'Sierra Grossa Hike', 'slug': 'sierra-grossa-hike-794012', 'price': 129.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 1.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/794012-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDYyMzR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1l3TDJnMVl5ODVOamMxTmpnek16TXlNVEkyTHpjNU5EQXhNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3wxNzMyZDJmYjBlYTMxMTFlYjE0NTMyYjAyMmQzMmJjYTU5NjcwMmM3N2U4NDJiNDBjN2NkMzA0YjU1ZGJjNDFl', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '794005', 'port_slug': 'alicante', 'title': 'Discover Elche, A UNESCO World Heritage City', 'slug': 'discover-elche-a-unesco-world-heritage-city-794005', 'price': 129.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<strong>City Exploration:</strong> Visit Elche known as the ‘Palm Forest of Europe’ and sample some delicious local delicacies. Set in the heart of Costa Blanca, the World Heritage site of Elche is surrounded by thousands of palm trees, which were originally introduced by the Phoenicians in around 300 BC. Enjoy a stroll along the paths between the lily-strewn ponds and the abundant plants in the Priest’s Garden. The Garden’s focal point is the magnificent 8 trunked ‘Imperial Palm’. Treat your taste buds to a specially prepared tasting of local produce such as dates, fig bread, dried apricots and date liqueur. In the old town center, a short visit will be made to the Basilica de Santa Maria, a blue-domed Baroque church built in the 17th century. Take approximately one hour of free time to explore Elche at your own pace. Stroll through the tranquil Municipal Park before departing back to Alicante.', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/794005-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNTE2NzN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1l5TDJnd1ppODVOamMxTmpjME1USTBNekU0THpjNU5EQXdOUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w5MjhlMGUyNzIzMTFlODZkY2FlZGM3MTEwOTU0MDYzMWZkMjljMjNhYWQ3MjBiNTMzZGExNjZkZTc1ODIzYjk3', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '794004', 'port_slug': 'alicante', 'title': 'Best of Alicante', 'slug': 'best-of-alicante-794004', 'price': 124.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Explore Alicante:</strong> Explore Alicante on a guided stroll that takes you through the charming old Moorish quarter, nestling at the foot of the imposing Castle. The Cathedral Church of Saint Nicholas has an austere renaissance façade, and inside you’ll discover a magnificent 17th century nave and 15th century cloister. See the impressive 18th century baroque Town Hall, where your guide will share details of its imposing exterior before some free time.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Santa Barbara Castle:</strong> Visit the Moorish Castle of Santa Barbara, one of Europe’s largest medieval fortresses. Set high on Benacantil Hill, gaze down from the castle battlements over the city and surrounding coastline. Enjoy a refreshing glass of sangria at a bar inside the castle.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>St. Faz Monastery:</strong> Discover the baroque-style Monastery of Santa Faz, with its pyramid-shaped dome. Inside the Monastery, discover a relic brought from the Vatican in the 15th century which, as tradition has it, is a cloth used by Christ to dry his bloodied face during the Stations of the Cross.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Free Time:</strong> Enjoy some time to explore the town on your own on the palm-lined Esplanade of Spain. Be sure to sample the local specialty, Horchata, a sweetened milk of crushed tiger nuts first introduced to Alicante by the Moors.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/794004-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMjExODJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREJpTDJnMk5DODVOamMxTmpjd09URXpNRFUwTHpjNU5EQXdOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w4MTlmZDZkZjc1OTU3Y2IyMmNhZjY3NGRlN2U0MzcwYTllZTRjNTQxYWUzOWMyODM2M2RmNzg0MTEzOTFkZjJi', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '794010', 'port_slug': 'alicante', 'title': 'Central Market and Tapas Tour', 'slug': 'central-market-and-tapas-tour-794010', 'price': 129.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Local Cuisine:</strong>Enjoy a tasting of tapas and discover the city by foot in the old quarter. The best place to experience Alicante’s gastronomy is at the Central Market to enjoy some tapas. The Mercado Central, as it’s called in Spanish, is an eclectic style building with modernist ornaments designed and built in 1921. This place is the main source of top quality, fresh and locally grown produce that includes meat, fish, vegetables, fruits, bread, pastries and flowers.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/794010-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTU3NjF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREU1TDJnMk9TODVOamMxTmpneE56STJORGswTHpjNU5EQXhNQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xmYzcyYTE5NzAxYTQxYzM2NzRiZDMwOTAyNWI5NTJiZTUwMTFiM2YzMDA3OGI1MDBlODU5YTBkNjM4Y2YwMDdl', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
