    {'code': '411026', 'port_slug': 'antigua', 'title': 'Antigua’s Tropical Beach Bliss', 'slug': 'antigua-s-tropical-beach-bliss-411026', 'price': 66.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.2, 'review_count': 29, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-beach-escape-antigua-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wxMDgxOTN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGtaQzlvTXpVdk9EZ3hNemt3T1RNeE1UVXhPQzVxY0djfGIxNzhjMGUxZjQ0NmJjODVkOTQzMTUzNjMzYzY2OGJiNzkxMDU5YzdlNjcxYzIwOTJjZThkYmZiNjczNTcwYWI&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '411051', 'port_slug': 'antigua', 'title': 'Historic Antigua & Beach', 'slug': 'historic-antigua--beach-411051', 'price': 102.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/411051-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTg5MzN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0U0TDJnd1l5ODVNREk0TmpFM09ETXdORE13THpReE1UQTFNUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w5MjE0ZWY3YWFmNmEwMzk4NzMxZDcyZWEyYWQ1OTM0NDVhOWRkY2Q5MTczOThkZWU5ZTIzMjE4NDA2ZjM0NjVl', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '412032', 'port_slug': 'aruba', 'title': 'Aruba’s Epic North Coast Jeep Adventure', 'slug': 'aruba-s-epic-north-coast-jeep-adventure-412032', 'price': 104.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.9, 'review_count': 9, 'desc_html': "<strong>Ayo Rock Formations:</strong> You will explore the Ayo Rock Formations, where you will find walking trails with several narrow tunnels all around. Your guide will walk the trails with you and give you some history on the rock formations and the island's earliest settlers. You will find ancient paintings carved into rocks by Caiquetio Indians from the Arawak Tribe.<br /> <br /> <strong>Natural Bridge:</strong> Stop at one of Aruba's most visited attractions, the Natural Bridge. Where once stood the magnificent Natural Bridge, naturally formed by coral limestone, before it collapsed in 2005, you can still see its ruins. There is another small bridge next to the ruins that is called the Baby Bridge, where you can walk on and take pictures.<br /> <br /> <strong>Bushiribana Gold Mill Ruins:</strong> See the remnants of a long-abandoned gold mill that processed gold ore during Aruba’s gold rush in the nineteenth century. You can get some stunning photos of the remains and backdrop of windswept waves crashing high along the coastline.<br /> <br /> <strong>Alto Vista Chapel:</strong> Visit the church and have an opportunity to sit in the church. This stop is a very spiritual place for the native inhabitants. Alto Vista means high view and this chapel was built in 1750 by the missionaries from South America that came to Aruba to convert the locals into Catholics.<br /> <br /> <strong>California Lighthouse:</strong> Drive by California Lighthouse, a silent watchman in the area known as Hudishibana, near the island's northwestern tip, named for the steamship California, which was wrecked nearby on September 23, 1891.<br /> <br /> <strong>Arashi Beach:</strong> The final stop will be at Arashi Beach, located on the northern tip of Aruba. Spend time on this calm and uncrowded beach to relax, go for a swim or snorkel.<br /> <br /> <strong>What’s Included:</strong></p> <ul> \t<li>Snack during tour.</li> \t<li>Bottled water and soda.</li> \t<li>Snorkel gear.</li> </ul>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/412032-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDUzOTR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1ZrTDJnME5pODVOakl6TVRJM016VTVOVEU0THpReE1qQXpNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w3YTA3MmRlODI5ZjJhODBjNGQ1OTA2OWRkYjA0YzU4MWQzZDkzNzVkNjI5N2ZhNTM1NDZmMWI2NmMwOWUwM2Q4', 'duration': '4.5 Hours', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': '4'},
    {'code': '412014', 'port_slug': 'aruba', 'title': 'Kukoo Kunuku Open Air Bus & Beach Break', 'slug': 'kukoo-kunuku-open-air-bus--beach-break-412014', 'price': 67.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.2, 'review_count': 24, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Kukoo Kunuku Bus Experience:</strong> Shake your maracas to the beat of Caribbean music on your open-air bus as you travel to the north coast. Catch the island spirit and get ready to paint the town red, on this wacky whimsical one of a kind bus. Along the way, enjoy views of the Aruba countryside, colorful cunucu houses and local fauna and wildlife as you learn a little about Aruba’s history and culture from your guide.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Alto Vista Chapel:</strong> Alto Vista means high view and this historic chapel was built in 1750 by the missionaries from South America that came to Aruba to convert the locals into Catholics. Guests will have the have an opportunity to visit and sit in the church.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>California Lighthouse:</strong> Stop for a picture and admire this charming lighthouse finished in 1916, situated on the north side of the island, that was built to signal ships nearing Aruba.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Beach Stop:</strong> Spend 2 hours soaking up the sun at one of Aruba’s stunning white sand beaches, such as Eagle Beach, Palm Beach, Arashi Beach, or Surfside Beach. Relax, swim in the crystal-clear waters, grab a meal or enjoy a refreshing Piña Colada under the shade of a palm tree.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>One hour narrated sightseeing tour.</li>\n\t<li>Complementary beach chair.</li>\n\t<li>Water.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/412014-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMjA1NjF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFZrTDJnell5ODVOakl6TVRJM05qZzNNVGs0THpReE1qQXhOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xiYjFkODFiNWQwMzkwY2FjYzk4MWMyZmU2MDYxOTgxYmYwNjc5Y2Q1OGUzMzhjYmZhYjJjMzYxNzczZDA0Mzkx', 'duration': '4.0 Hours', 'activity_level': 'Moderate', 'min_age': '5'},
    {'code': '412041', 'port_slug': 'aruba', 'title': 'Sailaway Snorkel & Palm Beach with BBQ Lunch', 'slug': 'sailaway-snorkel--palm-beach-with-bbq-lunch-412041', 'price': 119.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.4, 'review_count': 14, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Sailing Experience:</strong> Relax on a spacious custom-built catamaran, as you sail along the breathtaking coast of Aruba. Relax on lounge nets and take in the view of the white-sandy beaches and pristine shoreline. The certified guide will share fun facts and historical information about the excursion and island.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Snorkel at Catalina Bay:</strong> Stop at Catalina Bay, a pristine marine sanctuary with a large diversity of marine life featuring colorful angelfish, parrotfish, butterflyfish, surgeonfish, corals and much more. The snorkel instructor will provide you with National Geographic certified snorkel gear and knowledge about the marine life.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Snorkel at Antilla Shipwreck:</strong> Proceed to one of the largest shipwrecks in the Caribbean, the 400 ft. SS Antilla, a WWII German freighter, now home to an abundance of parrotfish, angelfish, butterflyfish, blue tangs, snappers, corals, sponges, sea fans and much more.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Leisure Time at Palm Beach:</strong> Following your lunch, enjoy one hour of leisure time to discover or just relax on Aruba’s white-sandy Palm Beach, while sipping on some Caribbean cocktails from the open bar. Your friendly guides will bring the drinks right to you on the beach or in the water. Afterward, your return bus will be prepared to take you back to the pier.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li style="list-style: disc !important; list-style-position: inside !important;">BBQ lunch.</li>\n\t<li style="list-style: disc !important; list-style-position: inside !important;">Open bar including Caribbean cocktails, water, sodas and fruit juices.</li>\n\t<li style="list-style: disc !important; list-style-position: inside !important;">National Geographic certified snorkel gear.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/412041-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTU3Mjl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFl4TDJoalpDODVOVFExTmpFek9EQXpOVFV3THpReE1qQTBNUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w5ZmExMTk2MTgxODdlNTU5YjIwYzdhZTU4YWJiYjcxMjNjMTI5ZTNhYjZkZGVmYzNhNTczZWY3NzE1ODQzZDlk', 'duration': '5.0 Hours', 'activity_level': 'Moderate', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '412027', 'port_slug': 'aruba', 'title': 'Eagle Beach & Aruba’s Must-See Highlights', 'slug': 'eagle-beach--aruba-s-must-see-highlights-412027', 'price': 81.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 5, 'desc_html': "<strong>The Tour:</strong> An entertaining and informative tour guide will take you around the colorful island in air-conditioned comfort. <br /><br /> <strong>Casibari Rock Formations:</strong> The rock formations are composed of quartz diorite formed million years ago. Evidence of prehistoric rock drawings is still visible at the formation. Guests can walk through the garden or climb to the top of the rocks for a stunning view with the ship in the background. <br /><br /> <strong>Baby Natural Bridge:</strong> This must-see scenery is a great stop for photos of the north coast! Current Baby Bridge was created by pounding waves and strong winds that slowly chiseled away the limestone cliffs along Aruba's north coast. Visit the snack bar and the gift shop for some unique souvenirs from Aruba. <br /><br /> <strong>California Lighthouse:</strong> Stop for 20 min at this iconic lighthouse, spanning from the north western most tip to downtown and see the cruise ships in the distance. Your tour guide will be at hand to help you get the perfect picture of you and your travel companions. <br /><br /> <strong>Eagle Beach:</strong> Stop at Eagle Beach for an hour and a half of leisure time to go for a walk or swim. You can rent a beach chair from a local beach vendor and relax while you sunbathe. <br /><br />", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/412027-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDIyMzJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREpoTDJobE15ODRPVGsxTVRVNE5qVTFNREEyTHpReE1qQXlOeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w4ZmQ5ODdiMzEyZTg2OWZkN2EwMGM0YzBkNDQ2MDM0MTY4MmIyZWU3NjVlM2IwNmFjNWM2N2VmODc0ZWUzZWMy', 'duration': '4.5 Hours', 'activity_level': 'Moderate', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '412089', 'port_slug': 'aruba', 'title': 'De Palm Island Snorkel, Beach, Aqua Park & Buffet', 'slug': 'de-palm-island-snorkel-beach-aqua-park--buffet-412089', 'price': 162.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 2.3, 'review_count': 7, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>De Palm Delights:</strong> Escape to De Palm Island, a coral island paradise offering all-inclusive fun for the entire family. Relax under a shaded palapa, join a lively salsa lesson, or check out some of the water activities. Indulge in a delicious lunch buffet featuring a grill station, complemented by an open bar for refreshing drinks.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Snorkel Adventure:</strong> Dive into the underwater paradise of De Palm with its stunning coral coastline and colorful reefs. Enjoy complimentary guided snorkel tours with gear, crystal-clear waters, and scenic ocean views while exploring the rocky shores.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Family Splash:</strong> Plunge into fun at the island's water park, featuring kid-friendly slides and splash areas perfect for younger guests, while thrill seekers can conquer the adrenaline-pumping Body Drop slides.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Buffet-style lunch.</li>\n\t<li>Open Caribbean bar.</li>\n\t<li>Snorkeling lessons.</li>\n\t<li>Snorkeling gear.</li>\n\t<li>Beach chairs.</li>\n\t<li>Access to Aqua Park.</li>\n\t<li>Salsa classes.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/412089-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDY1Njl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGt3TDJnNU1DODVNVE00TURrME5UQTJNREUwTHpReE1qQTRPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w5YjZjOGFiNzY3MWUxZjI2NmNjZDI5MmVhZDVhMzBiYmQzZGI3MmI0NzVmM2VjMzlmMWI5NDNiNzdjZTE4MjM5', 'duration': '6.0 Hours', 'activity_level': 'Moderate', 'min_age': ''},
