    {'code': '413077', 'port_slug': 'barbados', 'title': 'Bajan Vibes: Ocean Blues, Sand & Rum Punch', 'slug': 'bajan-vibes-ocean-blues-sand--rum-punch-413077', 'price': 79.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 4.7, 'review_count': 126, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/413077-img7.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyMzk5OTB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1kyTDJneE15ODVOekF3TXpjM01UTXpNRGcyTHpReE16QTNOeTFwYldjM0xtcHdad3wyYmUxMjdjZjBmZTZmNjY0NGUyNjAxYWRkMmQ3ZjllMGM2NGI0NTc4ZTIxN2ExNDlhOWIzY2YyZDlhMjJkYTJh', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '851017', 'port_slug': 'belfast', 'title': 'Belfast & Titanic Museum', 'slug': 'belfast--titanic-museum-851017', 'price': 174.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.5, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>City Highlights:</strong> Take a panoramic drive through Belfast, Northern Ireland’s largest city, passing iconic landmarks such as the Grand Opera House, Albert Memorial, Queen’s University, and the lush Botanic Gardens.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>A Symbol of Heritage:</strong> Admire the Renaissance-style City Hall, featuring a whispering gallery, a mural depicting Belfast’s historic industries, and the striking Titanic memorial statue, “Thane.”<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Titanic Experience:</strong> Visit Titanic Belfast®, an immersive six-floor museum at the historic shipyard where the Titanic was built. Learn about its construction, luxurious interiors, and the events leading to its tragic end.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Independent Explorations:</strong> Spend some free time at the slipways where Titanic was launched, enjoying breathtaking views, dining options, and shopping at the Titanic Store.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Return Journey:</strong> Rejoin your motor coach and take in more sights of the city as you head back to the ship, carrying with you the stories and history of Belfast.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/belfast-and-titanic-museum-851017-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNzA1MjJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzFNQzlvTTJJdk9EZ3hOamszTWpVeU9UWTVOQzVxY0djfDg4ZTNmZDM1ZDkwZjU4ZDFjZmY4YWY1NDc2ZjNmMWZmZWE4ODkxNzllZWFmZTk4NTdhMzI4ZjE1M2ZkMTZhZWI', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '851013', 'port_slug': 'belfast', 'title': 'Belfast City Walking & Pub', 'slug': 'belfast-city-walking--pub-851013', 'price': 194.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 3, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>A Walk Through Time:</strong> Stroll through the charming streets of Belfast, following its original 1660s layout, and immerse yourself in over 300 years of history and architectural splendor.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>City Hall:</strong> Marvel at the grandeur of Belfast’s City Hall, an iconic representation of the city's Victorian greatness and a gateway to its rich heritage.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Tracing Noble Roots:</strong> Walk past Castle Lane, once home to the Donegall family before their move to Belfast Castle, and explore the bustling Donegall Place, a hub of activity and history.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Albert Clock:</strong> Admire the Albert Clock, built in 1867, a distinctive leaning tower standing as a testament to Belfast’s past.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Titanic Legacy:</strong> Visit landmarks tied to Belfast’s Titanic history and hear stories of the people connected to this world-famous ship.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Pubs &amp; Social Traditions:</strong> Relax in one of Belfast’s finest pubs, where history, music, great food, and lively conversation create an unforgettable experience.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Murals of the Past:</strong> Drive through the famous Falls &amp; Shankill Roads, conditions permitting, and stop to photograph murals that depict Belfast’s turbulent history.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/belfast-city-walking-and-pub-851013-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNTk1NTd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzRaUzlvTURRdk9EZ3hOamMwTXpNMU1ETXdNaTVxY0djfDdhMjAwNmFmZGZlMGU2YzFhOWUzZjkyOTQ3OGI2ZDA1NzdkOGQyZmFiMTkwYjVlOTZhZTM5NjcyZjcwMWUwMTY', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '851029', 'port_slug': 'belfast', 'title': 'Game of Thrones Studio Tour', 'slug': 'game-of-thrones-studio-tour-851029', 'price': 269.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': 'Located at the authentic filming location of Linen Mill Studios in Banbridge, Northern Ireland, ‘Game of Thrones Studio Tour’ welcomes visitors into the Seven Kingdoms and beyond to explore the making of all eight seasons of HBO’s global hit series. Step onto original sets, including the iconic Great Hall at Winterfell where Jon Snow was proclaimed the “King in the North,” and view genuine set pieces including Daenerys Targaryen’s imposing Dragonstone throne. See first-hand the intricate detail of the costumes, weapons and props imagined by award-winning designers and artisans, and encounter interactive elements to relive some of the most memorable scenes from the show. Covering over 10,000 m2, this world-class attraction invites you to peek behind the scenes to discover all the elements that went into bringing the epic world of Game of Thrones™ to life.', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/851029-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDUyNjN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFZrTDJnell5ODRPVEk1TXpJNE5EazJOamN3THpnMU1UQXlPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wwOWU1Yjg5YTI5NTk1MjA4MzNmMjA3MzE5OWRlMDFiNWU0MTc3ZWQ2ZjVjYjRjZDEyMDEwZWMyMzljOTEwN2Iz', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '851032', 'port_slug': 'belfast', 'title': 'Belfast Combo – Giant’s Causeway & Titanic Belfa', 'slug': 'belfast-combo--giant-s-causeway--titanic-belfa-851032', 'price': 254.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Giants Causeway:</strong> Depart Belfast and embark on a scenic drive through Ballymena and Bushmills to reach the extraordinary Giants Causeway. Marvel at the rugged symmetry of the unique rock formations, which have withstood the test of time against Atlantic storms. Explore the newly opened Visitor Centre and immerse yourself in stories of mythology, geology, and history. After, venture to the basalt stones themselves, where you can let your imagination journey through ancient volcanic ages, or mythical legends.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Titanic Belfast:</strong> Immerse yourself in the fascinating story of the Titanic at Titanic Belfast®. Explore this state-of-the-art visitor experience, housed in a 6-floor iconic building, and discover the sights, sounds, and stories of the ship and the people who made her. Follow the themed one-way route to journey through the shipyard, the launch, and the maiden voyage as you uncover the hopes and dreams behind this world-famous tragedy. Take advantage of a short amount of free time to check out the slipways where the Titanic was launched, and then head over to one of the restaurants or cafés for a relaxing break before rejoining your motorcoach to the ship<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Professional English-speaking tour guide.</li>\n\t<li>Admission to Giant’s Causeway Visitor Centre including Audio Guides.</li>\n\t<li>Admission to Titanic Belfast including Audio Guides.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/851032-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDMwNjB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0pqTDJnM1pDODVNREkzTVRJeE1UZzBOems0THpnMU1UQXpNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w1NTRhMDZiMWJkNWY5ZDRiMjVhOThhYzg3NTMxMzY4NmJlOGIyZGY3Yjk3N2IxM2IyNDE0YWE4MjJkNmZmNDg1', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '851010', 'port_slug': 'belfast', 'title': "A Day in St. Patrick's Country", 'slug': 'a-day-in-st-patrick-s-country-851010', 'price': 229.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>City on the River:</strong> Begin with a short drive through Belfast, Northern Ireland’s vibrant capital, taking in its historic and modern landmarks.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>St. Patrick’s Centre:</strong> Explore an engaging exhibition that tells the story of Ireland’s patron saint, his mission, and the lasting impact of Irish missionaries across Europe.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Down Cathedral:</strong> Visit the striking Down Cathedral, home to St. Patrick’s grave, and learn about its historical significance in Irish Christianity.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Saul Church:</strong> See the replica of an early Christian church standing where legend says St. Patrick preached his first sermon in Ireland.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>A Taste of Strangford:</strong> Enjoy a meal in the picturesque village of Strangford, soaking in the scenic coastal surroundings while savoring local cuisine.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Portaferry Ferry Crossing:</strong> Take a short ferry ride across Strangford Lough, a stunning marine inlet known for its wildlife and natural beauty.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Grey Abbey:</strong> Explore the ruins of Grey Abbey, Ireland’s First Gothic Church, founded in 1193 by Cistercian monks, and admire its elegant yet simple stone carvings.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>A Seat of Power:</strong> Pass by Stormont, home to Northern Ireland’s Parliament, as you make your way back to the port.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/a-day-in-st-patricks-country-851010-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyODMzMjV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3hNUzlvTURZdk9EZ3hOVGsyTlRFeE1ETXdNaTVxY0djfDY0ODRhN2M5ZWFkNDEyYTQxMDkyNDg0NmYxNzk3ZGM5MzU2ZmJjNDllOWE4YWU0ZjA5Y2ZkNDZkYzUyNjBiYmY', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
