    {'code': '805012', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Cork Harbour by RIB and Irish Coffee', 'slug': 'cork-harbour-by-rib-and-irish-coffee-805012', 'price': 209.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': '/shop/medias/cork-harbour-by-rib-and-irish-coffee-805012-3.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNzAxMTJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3lZaTlvT1RJdk9EZ3lNRFE1TXpJNE56UTFOQzVxY0djfDg3YmExOGY1YzMzZmFmZTI1MWEwMTE2YWY4OGNlODlmZWNlZmY5ZmM1NTdiM2E2MzM2OTEyNTUzYzBjNjE1NmY&w=700&h=550&resize_profile=pdpgallery', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805001', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Full day Kerry Tour', 'slug': 'full-day-kerry-tour-805001', 'price': 189.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/full-day-kerry-tour-805001-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNjM4NTZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaG1ZUzlvTjJFdk9EZ3pNalkwTkRNNE1qYzFNQzVxY0djfGQ1YTdiYTdkMjY0NTRjN2Y0N2RiYjA0MzdlNjE2NDk1YmM4ODQ2NWM4OWNiZGYwZDdjYTk2ZjRiMDdjMDllNzk', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805003', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Kinsale and Charlesfort', 'slug': 'kinsale-and-charlesfort-805003', 'price': 129.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p>Your tour begins with a drive to Kinsale. On the way, you&rsquo;ll visit Charles Fort, an excellent example of a star-shaped fort built in the 1670s. Situated outside of Kinsale, Charles Fort spans 12 acres and boasts a lovely view of this pretty town from across an estuary. &nbsp;The fort was built in the time of Charles II (hence the name) and is a fine, almost unaltered example of 17th-century fortification, which follows the pattern of other fortified structures in Europe. Next, you&rsquo;ll return to the main road and travel to Kinsale and where you will have a short time for a photo stop. Kinsale is a quaint, little town, lying snug between hills and valleys and safely sheltered by the rounded contours of a beautiful harbor. It has enjoyed a reputation as a port of consequence, mainly through fishing and shipping. Kinsale has won several prizes &mdash; among them, the European Prize for Tourism and Environment, National Tidy Town and Gourmet Capital. Kinsale is steeped in history from its well-preserved medieval buildings and streetscapes, its 12th-century church of Multose and the 15th- century Desmond Castle, which houses the International Museum of Wine. Return to the ship in Cobh by passing through the City of Cork.&nbsp;</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/kinsale-and-charlesfort-805003-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTM4ODh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaG1OeTlvTW1Vdk9EZ3lNRFU0TWpnd09UWXpNQzVxY0djfDc1ZTRhYjU0MWRmYTRhOWIxY2EzYzQyZWU4ZDNkNWZlZDVmYzUyNWI3MDcxMDhlOTA4NGJhZjJiMGM3NWU3MTI', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805008', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Cork Walk', 'slug': 'cork-walk-805008', 'price': 144.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/cork-walk-805008-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDUwOTV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGtZeTlvWWpBdk9EZ3lNRFV3TkRNek1ESTNNQzVxY0djfGY2YmVhY2MxOTNmMjNkZDg5NTVlYmM2MjZkYTQ4ZDc3NGY1ZGY4OTkwM2QzMjMzYjUyYTE4YTMyZjUxZTIwZWQ', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805009', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Countryside & Kinsale', 'slug': 'countryside--kinsale-805009', 'price': 144.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 3.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/countryside-and-kinsale-805009-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTUyNzR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3lOUzlvT0Rndk9EZ3lNRFE1T0RnMU9EQXhOQzVxY0djfDcyMjU4NmVhZjE2OTk1MDQzNTY1ZDEyODc0NGZmMzhiY2Q0N2M5NWQxMmM1YTliZjcwNDU1MWIyMjUwOGI0YTE', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805007', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Discover Youghal and Lismore', 'slug': 'discover-youghal-and-lismore-805007', 'price': 134.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 3.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/discover-youghal-and-lismore-805007-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDM3MTJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3hNaTlvWmpNdk9EZ3lNRFV3TnpNeE1qRTFPQzVxY0djfGM4NGZiN2VmODMzZGY0YjcxNmRhMTliM2VmOGJiZTJhODlhMjI3YjM0N2MyNTE3MDIzN2RhYzZhODNiNmQ1ODg', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805004', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Waterford: City, County & Crystal with Lunch', 'slug': 'waterford-city-county--crystal-with-lunch-805004', 'price': 194.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>Departing from the cathedral town of Cobh, you will drive through East Cork to the neighboring County of Waterford. In Waterford, you&#39;ll visit the House of Waterford Crystal. Since the closure of the original factory in 2009, only a limited production of crystal occurs in Waterford. The new exhibition and showrooms will show you a the production process on a smaller scale with the finished product on display for you to view or perhaps purchase as a memento. A drive along the city&#39;s wharf will introduce you to Waterford&#39;s Viking roots. The city was settled by a Celtic tribe called the Deisi, and is still widely referred to as &ldquo;the Decies.&rdquo;. Recent archaeological excavations have revealed evidence of a Viking settlement there as early as the 10th century &mdash; not quite obliterated by the Anglo-Normans who followed. In fact, the city&#39;s English name comes from the Norse word, Vadrefjord. Following lunch at a local hotel, you will drive to Lismore. A brief stop allows you to photograph the spectacular Lismore Castle, the Irish home to the Duke of Devonshire and former home of Sir Walter Raleigh. Traveling through tranquil and picturesque countryside, you will then enjoy a leisurely drive back to Cobh and your waiting ship.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/waterford-city-county-and-crystal-805004-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDcwMjR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzFaQzlvWlRjdk9EZ3pNalkwTmpjME1qQTBOaTVxY0djfGNiNWIyNDgyYTY5OTg4ZWZjZGU3YjE4ZGNhZTM1NzkzYzFlMTQ3ODEzZmEwN2RlZjQ2NjE0ODcyMDUzZjkzMWE', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805002', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Half Day Lismore Castle Gardens', 'slug': 'half-day-lismore-castle-gardens-805002', 'price': 139.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/half-day-lismore-castle-gardens-805002-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNDU5MTd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGpOaTlvT0RZdk9EZ3pNalkwTlRjMU9UQXdOaTVxY0djfGVhZWE4MzZmZWMzZDQ2NDEyMmIzMGI4M2VkZmZmNWEzY2YzNmFhMWYyMDhiMWEzMGU0NTNmMzM3YTMxNTU3N2I', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805006', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Blarney Castle & Irish Coffee', 'slug': 'blarney-castle--irish-coffee-805006', 'price': 209.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 1.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/y01-blarney-castle-and-irish-coffee-805006-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNzg2MTR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzBOQzlvTm1Fdk9EZ3lNelEzTnpFM05ETXdNaTVxY0djfDgzY2M1ZjE3ZjJjMjZjMzA0MDlmZTY0ZTliYjBlZTQ2ZWYzOTE2ZWU2NGRkOTFmNjE4YmY3ZTJhOTg3ZTA3ZGQ', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805005', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Exploring Tipperary', 'slug': 'exploring-tipperary-805005', 'price': 229.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>From the ship, travel north to County Tipperary. Tipperary is Ireland&rsquo;s largest inland county, with richly varied, breathtaking scenery of hills, mountains, plains, and river valleys. Drive to Cashel and visit the rock that bears its name. The Rock of Cashel is an impressive pre-Christian settlement and the royal seat of the Kings of Munster from the 4th century AD. You will then have some free time in Cashel. Lunch will be served at a restaurant located beside the impressive rock. Then travel to Cahir, located on the River Suir. Cahir Castle, which dates back to the 15th century, was a stronghold of the powerful local Anglo-Norman Butler family and the dukes and earls of Ormond. The huge walls enclose three separate &ldquo;wards&rdquo;: the outer, middle and inner. The inner ward is guarded by a gate with a medieval portcullis. Rooms in the keep are whitewashed and contain armor displays and furnishings from the 16th and 17th centuries. Return to Cobh via the picturesque Vee Road, Lismore, Tallow and Midleton.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/exploring-tipperary-805005-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyMjkwNTZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzVOQzlvWVRZdk9EZ3lNRFV4TVRFM09EYzRNaTVxY0djfDE2ZTg3NTU0ZDQwN2M1NDA3ZDNhNGE5Mjc4MzZiMGEyYTE4YzM3MWFjYzgyM2NmZTkyYjEwYmM2OTA0ZjExMzc', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805018', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Best of Kerry & Killarney With Lunch', 'slug': 'best-of-kerry--killarney-with-lunch-805018', 'price': 199.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Kenmare:</strong> Sit back and relax as you traverse the idyllic countryside, dotted with quaint farms and villages, on your way to County Kerry. Prepare to be captivated by the Derrynasaggart Mountains’ ascent, leading you to Killarney National Park. Be mesmerized by the park’s magnificent lakes framed by lush trees and towering mountains and enjoy some leisure time exploring the charming town of Kenmare.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Muckross:</strong> Discover the allure of Muckross on this mesmerizing tour. Be mesmerized by the opulence of Muckross House, a 19th-century manor embraced by a magnificent rhododendron garden and sunken garden. Take a leisurely stroll through the gardens and immerse yourself in the breathtaking views of the stunning Killarney Lakes.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Killarney:</strong> Delight in a scrumptious 2-course lunch at a local restaurant before exploring the town and its enchanting shops independently before returning to Cobh.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>2 Course Lunch at local venue in Killarney Town.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/805018-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTY5MjF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1UyTDJneU1pODVNRE00TVRrNE1UYzNPREl5THpnd05UQXhPQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w4MzlmNjY2MTlkN2JmOWU2ZDI3NDQxYjQxZDZiNzYxNzUxYWE1ZWU2MTY5ODcwZTc5OTkyZmVjMGMyMDAzYTYy', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805020', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Private & Exclusive: Cork Cultural Show', 'slug': 'private--exclusive-cork-cultural-show-805020', 'price': 189.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Private Irish Music &amp; Dance Show:</strong> Delight in a private Irish music and dance show at the historic Commodore Hotel. Witness the vibrant energy of traditional dancers and the soulful beauty of Ireland’s cherished songs and stories.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Meet the Performers:</strong> Wrap up your experience by meeting the talented performers after the show. Enjoy a photo opportunity with the cast during a meet-and-greet!<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Admission to a private Irish music and dance show.</li>\n\t<li>Complimentary drink during the performance (beer, wine, or soft drink).</li>\n\t<li>Meet-and-greet with performers.</li>\n\t<li>Walking escort to and from the venue.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/805020-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTkwNDR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRE00TDJoak55ODVNVEExTXpJeE5Ua3dPREUwTHpnd05UQXlNQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xiOWI0OGIyNTE5ZWUwY2FhOTNkODMyZTVlMTViMzg3YWU1NmVjMjQwYzMyZTFmZjgwODQzYmZkMWUwZmIyMWIx', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805021', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Youghal Walk & Pub Visit', 'slug': 'youghal-walk--pub-visit-805021', 'price': 159.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Scenic Drive:</strong> Experience the beauty of County Cork on a scenic drive that takes you through delightful villages such as Castlemartyr and Killeagh, ending in the captivating coastal town of Youghal.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Youghal Stroll:</strong> Explore Youghal's picturesque beauty on a guided walking tour. Stroll along cobbled streets, admire medieval structures, and delve into the history of the town's impressive ancient walls.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Clock Gate Tower &amp; Market Square:</strong> Uncover the colorful history of the Clock Gate Tower and Market Square, featuring the 18th-century tower that served as a prison. A perfect blend of heritage and intrigue awaits!<br />\n<br />\n<strong>St. Mary’s Collegiate Church:</strong> Visit St. Mary’s Collegiate Church, one of the oldest active churches in Ireland, featuring striking Gothic architecture and exquisite stained glass. Be sure to see Sir Walter Raleigh’s tomb while exploring.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Local Pub Experience:</strong> Enjoy a refreshing drink at a cozy local pub and immerse yourself in the charm of this quaint town. You’ll also have time to explore its delightful streets and hidden gems at your own pace.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Guided walking tour of Youghal.</li>\n\t<li>Entrance to St. Mary’s Collegiate Church.</li>\n\t<li>One drink in a local establishment (beer, wine, or soft drink).</li>\n\t<li>Free time in Market Square.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/805021-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDE3NjB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGt3TDJobE1DODVNVEExTXpJeU1EUTVOVFkyTHpnd05UQXlNUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xiZjU0YjliOGU3NjA3MTUzYmQyOGZmMGQxYzM4YzA4YWU1NWI5N2ZiNzMzNTBhZWNhMWFkNTdiOGJlNTAzYTcw', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805019', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Cobh Combo – Kinsale, Blarney Castle & Jameson D', 'slug': 'cobh-combo--kinsale-blarney-castle--jameson-d-805019', 'price': 229.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Kinsale:</strong> Embark on a captivating journey through County Cork, where lush valleys, stunning coastline, and historic villages await. Discover the enchanting town of Kinsale, founded by the Anglo Normans and beloved for its naval heritage. Explore the streets lined with well-preserved 18th-century structures, Georgian homes, and Dutch-influenced architecture. Enjoy leisure time to browse shops, sample local delicacies, or unwind in a cozy pub, soaking up the town\'s unique atmosphere.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Blarney Castle:</strong> Experience the legendary charm of Blarney Castle as you lean backwards to kiss the famous Blarney Stone, said to grant the gift of eloquence. Explore the castle\'s impressive battlements and immerse yourself in the beautiful 18th-century "rock close" garden, believed to have ancient Druid roots.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Jameson Distillery:</strong> Step into the heart of whiskey-making tradition at the Jameson Whiskey distillery. Discover the history and craftsmanship of this beloved spirit as you tour the meticulously restored 18th-century industrial complex. Enjoy an audio-visual presentation, and if you’re selected, a sampling of their finished product, before unwinding in a cozy Irish pub with a glass of the finest whiskey. Don\'t forget to browse the souvenir store for unique keepsakes.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>English-speaking tour guide.</li>\n\t<li>Admission to Blarney Castle.</li>\n\t<li>Jameson Midleton Experience.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/805019-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDYwMjZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFU1TDJobVlpODVNREkzTVRJeU56STBPRGswTHpnd05UQXhPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w2OWZkZWVmNjBkYWNkNDVjYmE3ZDJlY2M3NDg5YWZiNTlhYjM3MGRmMTUyYTczYTU4N2M1ZmExY2YzODdlNGI1', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '805022', 'port_slug': 'cobh-cork', 'title': 'Cork Harbour Cruise', 'slug': 'cork-harbour-cruise-805022', 'price': 139.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Harbour Cruise:</strong> Embark on a Cork Harbour Boat Tour and cruise through one of the world’s largest natural harbors, surrounded by stunning landscapes and historic landmarks. Enjoy live commentary about the area’s maritime history, including tales of Spike Island, and sail past the picturesque towns of Cobh and Passage West. Keep your eyes peeled for wildlife, including seals and seabirds, as you soak in the beauty of this serene harbor.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Panoramic City Drive:</strong> After your cruise, enjoy a scenic coach tour through the lively streets of Cork City, immersing yourself in the essence of Ireland’s “Real Capital.”<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Scenic boat cruise through Cork Harbour.</li>\n\t<li>Live commentary from your local skipper guide.</li>\n\t<li>Panoramic coach tour of Cork City.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/805022-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDYzMjZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1l5TDJoalppODVNVEExTXpJeU5UQTRNekU0THpnd05UQXlNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xiOTA5YTc2MDllYjZmOTI0NDE5NTA3OTcxMzNhMzc2OWYzOTFkZjExMzNmMGQ4YmY0NDg0OWM1ZTkzYjI5ODU3', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '513015', 'port_slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'title': 'San Lorenzo Fortress & Agua Clara Locks', 'slug': 'san-lorenzo-fortress--agua-clara-locks-513015', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 10, 'desc_html': "<strong>Panama Canal & Agua Clara Locks Visitor Center:</strong> Experience a breathtaking journey to the iconic Panama Canal and Agua Clara Locks Visitor Center, renowned as the 8th wonder of the world. Witness the impressive operation of the Panama Canal in the state-of-the-art Agua Clara Visitor Center, offering a unique perspective on the New Locks & expansion project. Don't miss the chance to admire the canal's grandeur from the lookout area.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>San Lorenzo Fort:</strong> Embark on a thrilling 1-hour ride to San Lorenzo Fort, where you can relive the adventures of Captain Henry Morgan! Begin your journey with a scenic motorcoach ride through the lush rainforest, soaking in the natural beauty of Panama. Traverse a drawbridge across the new bridge over the iconic Panama Canal to reach the impressive San Lorenzo Fort. Take a captivating walking tour of this 16th-century fortress, immersing yourself in its rich history and marveling at the breathtaking views of the Chagres River and the Caribbean Sea. Discover fascinating tales of pirates and buccaneers that sailed these waters for centuries, including Captain Morgan's famous attack on San Lorenzo.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong>\n<ul>\n    <li>\n        A light snack with bottled water.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        The entrance fees to Agua Clara Locks.\n    </li>\n</ul>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-san-lorenzo-and-gatun-locks-colon-panama-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNTk3NzJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGlPUzlvT1dNdk9EZ3hOREF3TnpZME9ESTROaTVxY0djfGNmYmM3OTU2ZGFiNmVjYjZiMjMwYmRkYTczMGQ3MzczMDA2ZjM0NWRlODIxNGFmYzY2MmUyOTU3MTE0MjMzNGE', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
