    {'code': '513032', 'port_slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'title': 'Monkey Island on Gatun Lake', 'slug': 'monkey-island-on-gatun-lake-513032', 'price': 104.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.5, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/513032-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQ1MTF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGc1TDJnM015ODVNRE00TVRVeU5EazVNak13THpVeE16QXpNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w4OTE2YmE1OWE4YTE0MmFiZmQxODgwNTE0MmY4YTI2MTE3ZjE2YmI1OGYzOGM4ZDZkOTM2NzI4MDBkNDg2ZGMy', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '513033', 'port_slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'title': 'IMAX Theatre & Miraflores Locks', 'slug': 'imax-theatre--miraflores-locks-513033', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.8, 'review_count': 4, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/513033-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTMzOTN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1l6TDJnMk15ODVNRE00TWpBME5UWTNOVGd5THpVeE16QXpNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xlMmUwYmIzZjc2MDRlOGVjZTAyZWY0NzI1NDE3MWVmZmNjMDkxYWY2YTM5OGQ0NTZkM2UwM2U3NmNiOWNkNGIx', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '513034', 'port_slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'title': 'Explore it all from The Canal toThe Land', 'slug': 'explore-it-all-from-the-canal-tothe-land-513034', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 2.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>BEC Experience Center:</strong> Discover Panama's rich culture and flavors at the BEC Experience Center in Casco Antiguo, featuring world-class coffee, exquisite chocolate, and a taste of the nation's cherished beer through interactive tours and tastings.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Agua Clara Locks:</strong> Experience the engineering marvel of the Panama Canal at the Agua Clara Locks Visitor Center, where you can watch massive Neopanamax vessels navigate the state-of-the-art locks. Enjoy panoramic views from elevated platforms set within a lush, open-air park, and immerse yourself in the transformative impact of this monumental expansion on global trade.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Coffee, chocolate and beer samples.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/513034-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQ4ODF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREpqTDJnMFppODVNVE0zTlRNM05UUTRNekU0THpVeE16QXpOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wwOGUxNGIyZmUxZWYwYzkyZTBhODYyMmJmZjg3OGI2N2ExZWIyZWNjY2MyZTdlNWFhYWNjN2E4ZmM5YzdjYWFl', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '513019', 'port_slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'title': 'Kayaking the Panama Canal', 'slug': 'kayaking-the-panama-canal-513019', 'price': 114.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 1.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-kayaking-the-panama-canal-colon-panama-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNjM5MjN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaG1ZeTlvWkdJdk9EZ3hOREF3T0RVNU9EVTFPQzVxY0djfDQ0NmE0MTAzMDg4NmQ5NjhkOGUxYzk0NGVhNDM3YmQ0ODk4NzU1MTE1YzBlZDVkNDBiZGIzMjllYjQwYTNjMTM&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '513020', 'port_slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'title': 'Grand Tour: Eco Cruise, Indian Village & Locks', 'slug': 'grand-tour-eco-cruise-indian-village--locks-513020', 'price': 184.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.5, 'review_count': 8, 'desc_html': "<strong>Panama Canal & Agua Clara Locks Visitor Center:</strong> Experience a breathtaking journey to the iconic Panama Canal and Agua Clara Locks Visitor Center, renowned as the 8th wonder of the world. Witness the impressive operation of the Panama Canal in the state-of-the-art Agua Clara Visitor Center, offering a unique perspective on the New Locks & expansion project. Don't miss the chance to admire the canal's grandeur from the lookout area.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Jungle Eco Lodge:</strong> Escape to the heart of the rainforest with a 45-minute scenic drive to the Jungle Eco Lodge in Gatun Lake. Take in the lush greenery and vibrant wildlife before reaching the marina. Step onto a spacious catamaran and set sail across the tranquil waters of Gatun Lake, marveling at the untouched beauty of this natural paradise.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Gatun Lake Eco Cruise:</strong> Set off on an unforgettable voyage through the breathtaking Gatun Lake, where the beauty of the surrounding flora and fauna will take your breath away. Experience the wonder of the Panama Canal, a true marvel of human ingenuity. Gain a deeper understanding of its function and witness the incredible sights and sounds of this iconic landmark.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Rainforest Adventure:</strong> Immerse yourself in the natural wonders of Colon and the Panama Canal as you journey through a lush rainforest. Follow the majestic Chagres River as it winds its way to Gatun Lake, the lifeblood of the Panama Canal's locks system. Get up close and personal with the abundant wildlife that inhabits this breathtaking wonder.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Embera Indian Village:</strong> Step into the past and explore the untouched Embera Indian community as you traverse the rainforest. Transport yourself to the era of Vasco Nunez da Balboa's arrival in Panama, and be enthralled by the Neopono Puru performance, showcasing the captivating dances and showcasing the fascinating history and culture of the Gatun Lake community.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong>\n<ul>\n    <li>\n        The entrance fee to Agua Clara Locks.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        A light snack with bottled water.\n    </li>\n</ul>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-grand-tour-eco-indians-and-locks-colon-panama-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyODI1NzV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaG1PQzlvTnpBdk9EZ3hOREF3T0RjMk1qTTVPQzVxY0djfDM0M2VkYTFlMWUzNjE1YTNmMTI0ZmVkYTg0ZGYxMTc5ODZkMDIxMWU1OWM0NDgyZjI1MTc0NDgyM2M4OTI4MWU', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '513005', 'port_slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'title': 'Panama Canal Tour', 'slug': 'panama-canal-tour-513005', 'price': 204.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.1, 'review_count': 22, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-panama-canal-tour-colon-panama-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wxNTc5MTl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3lZeTlvTlRjdk9EZ3hOREF3TmpnMk1UZzFOQzVxY0djfDZmZmNiOGFmNjNjZDE5ODAzNmM5YjgwYWQxMzQ1YjZhZWY5YzVmMTQ2YjI5MDQyMDE3ZGI0MWVhMWM1MGYyNWE&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '513009', 'port_slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'title': 'Two Oceans by Railroad', 'slug': 'two-oceans-by-railroad-513009', 'price': 199.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.5, 'review_count': 11, 'desc_html': "<strong>Isthmian Railroad:</strong> Embark on an unforgettable journey as you traverse the Isthmian Railroad, the world's first Trans-Continental railroad. Marvel at the breathtaking views of two oceans in just one hour, departing Colon City on the Caribbean Coast and crossing the Continental Divide to the Pacific side. As you travel alongside the majestic Panama Canal, soak up the rich stories of legendary figures like Christopher Columbus and Ferdinand de Lesseps, while being treated to the stunning vistas of the Gatun Lake and the vibrant rainforest.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Agua Clara Locks & Old Canal Zone:</strong> Experience the awe-inspiring Panama Canal Expansion as you witness the construction of the New Locks, doubling the Canal's capacity. Be a part of this historic endeavor by visiting the Observation Center, a park-style concept offering a unique vantage point to observe the vessels crossing. With its open platforms and roofed terraces, the center can accommodate up to 400 visitors, allowing everyone to marvel at the majestic Gatun Lake and watch as ships navigate through the canal.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong>\n<ul>\n    <li>\n        Train ticket.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        Entrance fees to Agua Clara Locks.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        A light snack with bottled water.\n    </li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/513009-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNjkxNzN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGM0TDJoaFpDODVNRE0zTURFd05UTTBORE13THpVeE16QXdPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w1MTMyMDRjNTMwZDYzMzI1NTU1NzU4NDI0Y2ZjMDdmZDJhODZmZjY5ZjMxZWY3MjMwMjg2NWIwMzU5Y2Y5NDIw', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '513023', 'port_slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'title': 'Panama City Tour', 'slug': 'panama-city-tour-513023', 'price': 94.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 2.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': '<strong>Scenic Drive:</strong> Kick-start your adventure with a comfortable 90-minute bus ride to Panama City, the vibrant capital of Panama.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Old Panama:</strong> Explore the historic ruins of Old Panama, founded in 1519, on a 1-hour guided tour inside the Visitor Center. Discover the fascinating history of this site as you visit the museum and witness the well-preserved ruins.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Colonial City:</strong> Discover the rich history of Casco Antiguo on a 1-hour guided walking tour. Founded in 1673 after being destroyed by Captain Henry Morgan, this charming colonial city is filled with fascinating historic monuments. Explore the Cathedral Plaza and stroll along the legendary Las Bovedas, adorned with engravings recounting the history of the French Canal. Enjoy 15 minutes of free time at the end of your visit to soak in the beauty of this remarkable destination.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong>\n<ul>\n    <li>\n        Entrance fees to Old Panama.\n    </li>\n    <li>\n        A light snack and a bottled water.\n    </li>\n</ul>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/513023-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDU5MDJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGt6TDJnNVppODVNRE0zTURBM016SXpNVFkyTHpVeE16QXlNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w1ZTAwNjNjYWFkOTlhMDBhNjkzZGIwZDAyNzcyMTkyZDFlZmIzNmU3YTQ2ZmVkNjYyOGNmOWFjYjM1ZTFiYTU4', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '513018', 'port_slug': 'colon-panama-canal', 'title': 'Eco Cruise & Agua Clara Locks', 'slug': 'eco-cruise--agua-clara-locks-513018', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.8, 'review_count': 6, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y05-eco-cruise-and-gatun-locks-colon-panama-5.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMjY4MzB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzBOUzlvTkdFdk9EZ3hOREF3T0RRMk56UTROaTVxY0djfDVkZTk5MTNmYmFmMjVhNjk3MjkxMmVkZGZlMDY4ZGFiZTA3ZjhjYmQzYzUxYzAxODQzMmI4NzU0YmRjYjJlZDM&w=700&h=550&resize_profile=pdpgallery', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '355010', 'port_slug': 'coquimbo-la-serena', 'title': 'La Serena & The Third Millenium Cross', 'slug': 'la-serena--the-third-millenium-cross-355010', 'price': 119.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Third Millennium Cross:</strong> Leave the port of Coquimbo, passing through the downtown area en route to the stunning Third Millennium Cross. Take in remarkable 360-degree views of the city and its surroundings before continuing your northward journey.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>La Serena’s Coastal:</strong> Travel along the beautiful coast to La Serena, where you will find contemporary hotels, clubs and lively restaurants beside expansive beaches. Capture moments at the historic lighthouse and cruise along Avenue Francisco de Aguirre, showcasing classical marble statue replicas.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>La Recova:</strong> Take a few moments to stroll to La Recova, a lively market where you can find a wide range of gifts and souvenirs, including jewelry crafted from lapis lazuli, a local semi-precious stone, before rejoining your bus.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Hilltop Sights:</strong> Conclude your visit with a panoramic photo opportunity at the hilltop near La Serena University, offering stunning views of the city. The tour then takes a scenic return to Coquimbo along the Pan-American Highway.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Entrance fees to Third Millennium.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/355010-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQyNzN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR00yTDJoa1lpODVNVE14TnpZeU1EVTNNalEyTHpNMU5UQXhNQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wyZGIyN2ExMWI2YzEzODI5OTNmZDczYmQyYWMyZDc2NzEzMTgxZmI3NDQwNmViN2JhMDdlODdiOTdiYTNiYTYw', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '355005', 'port_slug': 'coquimbo-la-serena', 'title': 'Petroglyphs Discovery: Winery Tasting & Lunch', 'slug': 'petroglyphs-discovery-winery-tasting--lunch-355005', 'price': 239.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Scenic Journey:</strong> Leave the pier and head into the scenic Limary Valley, where misty hills give way to beautiful ranchlands, rolling farms, and vibrant vineyards. Experience the captivating charm of this picturesque landscape.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Wine Tasting:</strong>&nbsp;Experience a distinguished local winery as you explore the grounds and learn about traditional winemaking practices in Chile. Finish your visit with a tasting of three handcrafted wines.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Enchanted Valley:</strong> Make your way to the Enchanted Valley, an extraordinary open-air museum located in the desert. Enjoy a guided walk through cactus-lined trails and discover the rock formations that reveal the history of the nomadic El Molle Culture.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>A Taste of Chile:</strong> Delight in a classic Chilean lunch that highlights the region's unique flavors. Pair your meal with a refreshing Pisco Sour, a signature Chilean cocktail made with grape brandy, citrus, and aromatic bitters.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Entrance fee to the Enchanted Valley.</li>\n\t<li>Local wine sampling: 3 types of wines.</li>\n\t<li>Lunch at a local venue.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/ComingSoonEurope-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTkzNTl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFF4TDJoak9TODRPVEV4T0RVMk5UQXdOelkyTDBOdmJXbHVaMU52YjI1RmRYSnZjR1V0YVcxbk1TNXFjR2N8OTQwYzM1ZTMxNWE5NmViNjI1N2E5OTNlZWUxNGI4NGU5ZmIyYjg3MDY5ZTNhOWM1NDNjNzQxNzI3M2ZiZDNhMg', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '355006', 'port_slug': 'coquimbo-la-serena', 'title': 'From Coast to Cellars: Pisco & Elqui Valley', 'slug': 'from-coast-to-cellars-pisco--elqui-valley-355006', 'price': 199.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Scenic Drive:</strong> Depart from Coquimbo and enjoy a scenic drive along the coastal promenade to La Serena. Stop to admire the historic lighthouse, a symbol of the city, and capture memorable photos along the way.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Pisco Traditions:</strong> Continue your journey into the Elqui Valley to visit a famous distillery known for Chile's national spirit, Pisco. Tour the cellars and exhibition rooms to learn about the production process and enjoy a tasting of this celebrated local drink.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Independent Explorations:</strong> Explore the charming town of Vicuña, the heart of the Elqui Valley. Enjoy free time to visit the main square, see the historic Bauer Tower, explore the local church, and browse the vibrant handicraft market.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Refresh &amp; Reflect:</strong> Wrap up your day with light refreshments served at a nearby restaurant before returning to the pier for departure.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Pisco distillery sampling and wine sampling.</li>\n\t<li>Snack at a local venue.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/355006-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNjY1MzV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGs0TDJnek1TODVNVE14TnpVM05qWTJNek0wTHpNMU5UQXdOaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xiNTg3YzM4MTU5OTU2YmQ3NzhlMWFmMGVhZTI0M2UwNzFjNTQzNmNlZTZmOGE5NDdhY2FjMDZjZGZkMGVhMzM0', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '355008', 'port_slug': 'coquimbo-la-serena', 'title': 'Explore La Serena at Your Pace', 'slug': 'explore-la-serena-at-your-pace-355008', 'price': 89.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/355008-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTQxNzV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1F5TDJobU1DODVNVE14TnpVNU1EYzFNelU0THpNMU5UQXdPQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wwNGU0Zjk4OTI2MjQwZTFmYzBmOTYwY2MwZmFkOTdkZTEwZDY2YWQzOTYyMWJkNjRlOTliNjkyYjM0ZDgwNzBl', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '355007', 'port_slug': 'coquimbo-la-serena', 'title': 'A Panoramic La Serena Journey - Shores & City View', 'slug': 'a-panoramic-la-serena-journey--shores--city-view-355007', 'price': 79.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/355007-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTkxOTR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREEzTDJnNU5DODVNVE14TnpVNE5ERTVPVGs0THpNMU5UQXdOeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3wwYTY3YjA3YWI2ZmM0YWMwZjU3YmFhMDk3ZGE0YzAwNjBmMTUzZWJkNDFiNzRlNmUwNTIzYTNkZjVjMzlmZGY2', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '355009', 'port_slug': 'coquimbo-la-serena', 'title': 'Coquimbo & La Serena: Chile’s Coastal Icons', 'slug': 'coquimbo--la-serena-chile-s-coastal-icons-355009', 'price': 109.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Avenida del Mar:</strong> Depart the pier and travel along Avenida del Mar, a 12-kilometer coastal road known for its beautiful beaches and vibrant atmosphere. Experience the lively environment filled with hotels, restaurants, pubs, nightclubs, and lush gardens as you make your way to La Serena.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>City Symbol:</strong> Visit the Monumental Lighthouse, a 28-meter-high symbol of the city constructed in 1951. You will have time to capture photos of the picturesque beaches alongside this historic structure.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Marble Marvels:</strong> Continue your tour down Francisco de Aguirre Boulevard, which showcases reproductions of historic marble statues scattered among the trees in this well-loved park.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Archaeological Museum:</strong> Discover La Serena's historic downtown, founded in 1544, starting at the Main Square. Walk three blocks to the Archaeological Museum, housed in a building from 1945, and explore an impressive collection of pre-Hispanic artifacts, including Diaguita pottery.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>La Recova:</strong> Take a few moments to stroll to La Recova, a lively market where you can find souvenirs, local items such as papayas, and handcrafted goods before rejoining your bus. You will then proceed back to the pier using the inner road.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Entrance fees to the Archaeological Museum.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/355009-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTI4MDd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFF3TDJobU1DODVNVE14TnpVNU9Ua3lPRFl5THpNMU5UQXdPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xlZTJlMWRlMzc1N2ExNzkxNzAzNTU3YjQ1NjZkMjk0NWUzNmQ3NmRmZDBhMjA4YWU3NWY5OWViNzcyOTFmNTQ5', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '865004', 'port_slug': 'corfu', 'title': 'St Michael, St George Palace & Paleokastritsa', 'slug': 'st-michael-st-george-palace--paleokastritsa-865004', 'price': 139.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>Corfu is undoubtedly the greenest and one of the prettiest of the Greek islands with rows of cypress, orange, lemon and olive groves as well as vineyards that grow amidst grassy fields studded with colorful wildflowers. Begin this exploration of Corfu with a visit to the Museum of Asian Art. Housed in what was once the St. Michael &amp; St. George Palace, this neo-classical building was completed in 1824 and served as the headquarters of the British High Commission during the years of British rule of the Ionian Islands. The building has been a museum since 1927 when Ambassador Gregory Manos donated his 10,500-piece collection of Sino-Japanese art, the foundation of the museum’s exhibits. Admire the impressive throne room, the ballroom and the dining room where the walls are decorated with medals of chivalric orders of bygone eras. Then stroll through Corfu’s Old Town, visit Saint Spyridon Church (the island\'s patron saint), and admire its important religious collections. Then walk along the narrow streets of the town, beneath the picturesque balconies and archways, past the Town Hall and cricket pitch (central strip of the cricket field), which is still in use today. Rejoin the motorcoach for the drive to Perama and admire wonderful views across the bay and Mouse Island from the Monastery of Vlacherna. Enjoy a break for lunch at a traditional Greek restaurant that offers Corfiot specialties. Then it is on to Paleokastritsa, often referred to as "Corfu\'s Capri". Paleokastritsa is a dramatic natural harbor protected by a rocky cliff and laced by a golden sandy beach. Here, you will have time to take photos and browse in the village’s little shops or have a quick coffee. A brief stop is made at the Monastery of the Holy Virgin to admire the views before returning to the ship.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Achillion-Palace-Paleokastritsa-with-Lunch-HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMzM4Njh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGtZeTlvTTJRdk9EZ3hNems1TkRNeE1UY3hNQzVxY0djfDg0NDk0NWI4Y2M3M2U0MGU2YjUzZmU0ZGU0MjhjYTUxMzY0OWYwYzBlYzY1YzA1ZGRhYjk2N2JkZWI5ZDI0YzI', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '865003', 'port_slug': 'corfu', 'title': 'Hidden Villages by 4WD', 'slug': 'hidden-villages-by-4wd-865003', 'price': 134.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>Meet your guide and lead driver at the port, who will explain the details of the panoramic drive. Join your 4x4 vehicle and follow the lead vehicle as you head along the main coastal road towards the island\'s north coast, passing the popular resorts of Alykes and Kontokali. Through Gouvia, the drive continues past the villages of Agios Vassilios and Ano Korakiana before taking a narrow winding road that passes through Sokraki. Perched on a mountain peak and surrounded by pine and olive trees, this is one of oldest villages on the island. The drive continues towards the village of Troumbettas, along a mountain ridge with spectacular views of the islands of Mathraki and Othoni that mark the northwestern tip of Greece. From Troumbettas, follow a narrow country lane passing by the villages of Alimatades, Vistonas and Makrades on the way to "Castellino" restaurant. Located high up in the village of Lakones, this restaurant is renowned for its breathtaking panorama view over the Bay of Paleokastritsa. Here, time to indulge in a typical Greek meze and a glass of wine. From Lakones, descend to Paleokastritsa Bay, also known as "Corfu\'s Capri": a natural harbor with a sandy beach that is entirely protected by a rocky cliff. According to Homer’s Odyssey, this is the bay where Odysseus was shipwrecked and where he met Nausica. From Paleokastritsa, return to Corfu port.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Hidden-Villagess-by-4WD-HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDA2NTR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzJZeTlvWXpjdk9EZ3hNems1TkRFME56ZzNNQzVxY0djfDJjOTI5ZWE1ZjU4ZDVhZDMzNDJkYTI2MWE0ODM1YmZjNTg3MTE2YWIzYzhjNDQ4NTgwYzk1OGRiNTFkNzUwY2E', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '865010', 'port_slug': 'corfu', 'title': 'Heritage Town & Paleokastritsa Monastry with Swimi', 'slug': 'heritage-town--paleokastritsa-monastry-with-swimi-865010', 'price': 79.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>Explore the beauty of Corfu, with a visit to Paleokastritsa and to the heritage town of Corfu. This leisurely tour begins with a scenic drive through the lush green countryside to Paleokastritsa, famous for the crystal blue-green sea of its beaches, the mysterious grottoes, the impressive rocks and bays, that form one of the most beautiful settings in Greece. Stop at one of the beautiful coves and discover Paleokastritsa’s stunning beauty and experience one of its wonderful beaches for a swim in the crystal-clear sea. Next, visit the Monastery of Paleokastritsa, founded in 1226, to see its splendid church, its shady arcaded cloisters and its inviting gardens, all exuding a deep sense of peace. Continue with a scenic drive to the heritage Old Town of Corfu, to enjoy a walking tour. UNESCO’s World Heritage Sites list the Old Town as a fortified Mediterranean port town of high integrity and authenticity. Discover all the interesting sites such as the Saint Spyridon Church, the charming narrow alleyways of the old Venetian town, the famous Esplanade, notably one of the largest squares in Europe. Pass by elegant Liston, the Town Hall and the imposing Palace of St. Michael and St. George. Before returning to the bus and to the port, enjoy free time for shopping and strolling.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/865010-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDc4OTd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR001TDJneU5DODRPVEl5TWpJNU5UY3hOakUwTHpnMk5UQXhNQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xmMjM4NGJhMjkzMmE2NWE1ZDEzZjNkMDM5NzBlZTE4MzEyNGViYzVmZjAyYmIyMDkxZDdhMTc1YTk2MGY4Y2Uz', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '865007', 'port_slug': 'corfu', 'title': 'Paleokastritsa, Mon Repos & Corfu Town', 'slug': 'paleokastritsa-mon-repos--corfu-town-865007', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p>Just south of Corfu Town is the majestic Estate of Mon Repos. Perched on the coast, this 258-acre parkland was first developed in 1828 as the estate and residence of the British High Commissioner, Frederick Adams. The villa, at the estate’s highest point, has gardens with a plethora of local and exotic flora, to enjoy. This was also the birthplace of Prince Philip, the Duke of Edinburgh, who was born here in 1921. After extensive renovations, the villa was converted to a museum. From there you will enjoy beautiful views from the hill of Analipsi, the ruins of the ancient city and the basilica of Palaiopolis. Then, continue to the Old Town of Corfu to enjoy a walking tour of its picturesque streets. Boasting Venetian fortifications, neo-classical buildings and charming houses, the Old Town is described in UNESCO’s World Heritage List as a fortified Mediterranean port town of high integrity and authenticity. Admire the famous Esplanade, one of Europe’s largest squares, and the elegant Liston which once allowed access only to the aristocracy of Corfu. Discover all the interesting sites including Saint Spyridon Church, the island’s protector, Town Hall and the charming narrow alleyways that crisscross larger, bustling streets that abound with typical craftsmen’s workshops and colorful shops. Leave the town behind and head north to Paleokastritsa, also known as "Corfu\'s Capri", a sandy beach in a stunning natural harbor that is entirely protected by a rocky cliff. Visit Paleokastritsa\'s venerable monastery, founded in 1226. Enjoy the peaceful atmosphere created with shady archways and lovely gardens and admire the pretty bays of Paleokastritsa before returning to the port.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Paleokastritsa-Mon-Repos-Corfu-Town-HERO.JPG?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzNjMzNTV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzBOQzlvTkRZdk9EZ3hNems1TlRJMk1UazRNaTVxY0djfGQwMzliODk4MmE4MzQ1MTc0YzJhNzVkYzI3YjU4YzQyOTkzZjcwYjI5OWU0ZmUyZDA4YWI1NTUxNjQyMTRiZjU', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '865008', 'port_slug': 'corfu', 'title': 'Highlights of Corfu by Land & Sea', 'slug': 'highlights-of-corfu-by-land--sea-865008', 'price': 124.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p>Start your introduction to Corfu with a guided walk through the historic Old Town and the island’s capital. Boasting Venetian fortifications, neo-classical buildings and charming houses, the Old Town is described in UNESCO’s World Heritage List as a fortified Mediterranean port town of high integrity and authenticity. Admire the famous Esplanade, one of Europe’s largest squares, and the elegant Liston, which once allowed access only to the aristocracy of Corfu. Built on the side of a hill, the town is made up of a small alleyways crisscrossing with larger, bustling streets that abound with typical craftsmen's workshops and colorful shops. Discover all the interesting sites that include Saint Spyridon Church, dedicated to the island’s protector, Town Hall and the charming Old Town. Then continue with a scenic drive through the lush green countryside to Paleokastritsa, famous for the crystal blue-green sea and its beaches, mysterious grottoes, impressive rock formations and coves, that create one of the most beautiful locations in Greece. It is here that archaeologists believe the legendary castle of King Alkinoos was built as is recorded in the writings of Homer. Stop at one of the beautiful bays, where you will sail on a small boat to see three impressive small caves, Nausica, St. Nicholas and the Blue Eye. The boat trip continues to the other side of Paleokastritsa, where the wonderful jagged coastline of this stunning location can be enjoyed. Discover the deep blues of the Ionian Sea during this unforgettable experience! After this little cruise, spend some free time at leisure for swimming or exploring Paleokastritisa before returning to Corfu port.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Highlights-of-Corfu-by-Land-Sea-1.JPG?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTY5NTZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGtaaTlvWXpNdk9EZ3hNems1TmpBeE5UWTBOaTVxY0djfDJmNDkyMzBiYWFhOTVhZThjMDk4Y2FjNTE0MzRhZjg2MDgwZGVmM2YzNWVhZjY3MWE2MDk5M2NmZWU0YWRkYjY', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
