    {'code': '888016', 'port_slug': 'dun-laoghaire-dublin-ireland', 'title': 'EPIC: The Irish Emigration Story', 'slug': 'epic-the-irish-emigration-story-888016', 'price': 169.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/888016-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDc5NTB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGhtTDJobU15ODRPVEk0TkRJeU1EWTRNalUwTHpnNE9EQXhOaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w4ZGUyMDEwZjk5MWZlMDgyOGI4YmU5YWRkZjc3ODg3YzIyYmEyNzJkZDRiMDY1ZGEzMGJkZmZmNjFiZTJhMDg5&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '888013', 'port_slug': 'dun-laoghaire-dublin-ireland', 'title': 'A Taste of Dublin: On the Trail of Fabulous Food', 'slug': 'a-taste-of-dublin-on-the-trail-of-fabulous-food-888013', 'price': 279.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 1.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/888013-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTk4NDV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREZsTDJneU55ODRPVEk0TkRJd01qazROemd5THpnNE9EQXhNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xmYjRjOTE4ZWViNjVlMzU0NzljZDEyZWYxODcwZTlmYjBhYTc4NGI0M2U1MmZkYjg0ZjIwOWU0ZDUwNDE1YWZh&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '888011', 'port_slug': 'dun-laoghaire-dublin-ireland', 'title': 'The Guinness Experience', 'slug': 'the-guinness-experience-888011', 'price': 189.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 1.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': "<p>Departing the harbor town of Dún Laoghaire, your drive will take you into the heart of bustling Dublin, Ireland's capital city – steeped in ancient history and youthful energy. On a panoramic orientation drive through town, you will see the Old Parliament House, Trinity College founded in 1592 by Queen Elizabeth I, and Merrion Square, one of Dublin's grandest Georgian squares and now the address of the National Gallery of Ireland and the Irish Parliament. View Georgian Dublin, the National Gallery of Ireland and St. Stephen's Green. You'll also pass Dublin Castle, City Hall, Christ Church Cathedral and St. Patrick's Cathedral. At the Guinness Storehouse Museum, The Guinness Experience tells a dramatic story that begins more than 250 years ago. Often surprising and always entertaining, the adventure starts the moment you walk through the door. As you make your way through the Storehouse Museum, you'll discover what goes into making the 'black stuff' – the ingredients, the process, the passion. The tour ends at Gravity, the sky bar where you will be treated to a pint of Guinness.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/888011-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNTUzODJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGN3TDJoaU9TODRPVEk0TkRFNE9ESTBNakl5THpnNE9EQXhNUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wwOWQzNGM0YjVjZDkzYTQ0MTJmMjI3NGFhMzQwNzlmOGJjY2UxMWI5NDlkZjlkZDkzZTZiMTExMzY2ZTJiNWM5', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '888012', 'port_slug': 'dun-laoghaire-dublin-ireland', 'title': 'A Walk through Dublin', 'slug': 'a-walk-through-dublin-888012', 'price': 149.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': "<p>Transfer to the center of Dublin, where your guided walking tour begins at Merrion Square in the heart of this Georgian capital. The first impressive building you will view is the National Gallery of Ireland, which contains many fine works by El Greco, Goya, Gainsborough and Caravaggio (among others). Continuing your walk, you’ll pass the Government Buildings and the Huguenot Cemetery before arriving at St. Stephen's Green. This open space consists of 22 acres of beautifully laid out and manicured parkland. It is a familiar and much-loved backyard to all Dubliners. Walking down Dawson Street, you will pass Mansion House – residence of Dublin's Lord Mayor. Cross over to Grafton Street, Dublin's fashionable shopping strand, and you'll stop at a typical Irish pub. This is a chance to order a cool pint of Ireland’s most famous and darkest stout beer (or another beverage of your choice) and meet some of the 'Dubs', as the locals are known. Take time to stroll through independently or perhaps browse the shops during free time. At the conclusion of your tour, meet up with your guide and return to Merrion Square and the waiting coach.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/888012-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDU4NTZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFZsTDJobE15ODRPVEk0TkRFNU5qUXpOREl5THpnNE9EQXhNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w2ODI1ZjYzNmQxMmI1MjQ3YjgyMzdkMTM0ZTA3MTY4MzNiNmIyYmY5NDk2YmQ3MzM3ZjgxZTYyMGZhNGJiMjRi', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '888015', 'port_slug': 'dun-laoghaire-dublin-ireland', 'title': 'Teeling Distillery & Panoramic of Dublin City', 'slug': 'teeling-distillery--panoramic-of-dublin-city-888015', 'price': 184.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p>On a panoramic drive through Dublin, you will see the Old Parliament House, which is now the Bank of Ireland. Continue past Trinity College, founded in 1592 by Queen Elizabeth I, and the Georgian squares of Merrion and Fitzwilliam. Watch for sprawling St. Stephen's Green, Dublin Castle, City Hall, Christchurch Cathedral, St. Patrick's Cathedral and Guinness – home of the world's most famous brew.</p>\n<p>The Teeling Distillery is located in the heart of the city and is the first new whiskey distillery to open in Dublin in more than 125 years. Here, you will enjoy a fun and informative guided tour and tasting. Immerse yourself in more than 300 years of whiskey history – the rise and fall and rise (again) of the Dublin whiskey industry makes for a fascinating story. You'll take a guided tour of the operational distillery, learning about all five crucial steps in the whiskey-distilling process. Wouldn't it seem rude to leave without tasting the product? Of course, it would! You're invited to sample four whiskeys, including the Distillery Exclusive whiskey, not available anywhere else. The new single-pot still whiskey is one of the few whiskeys made in Dublin in more than 40 years.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/888015-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDU5NTh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRE5tTDJnNVlTODRPVEk0TkRJeE5URXhNVGs0THpnNE9EQXhOUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w0NGFjNGU5MmU1NmM4NGNlNjkxYjJiYTIzMjg5NDExMjY3Y2NiOTUyZGYxNWVhNTE3ZGMwOGUwM2FjYWE3ZGIx', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '888014', 'port_slug': 'dun-laoghaire-dublin-ireland', 'title': 'Easy Dublin', 'slug': 'easy-dublin-888014', 'price': 149.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': "<p>Departing from the pier in the harbor town of Dun Laoghaire, your guide and driver will take you to the heart of bustling Dublin City. As you reach the city on your panoramic drive, you will soon spot the National Gallery of Ireland and various government buildings. You will stop to photograph the world-famous Doorways of Dublin in Fitzwilliam Square. Pass Dublin Castle, City Hall and Christchurch Cathedral en route to St. Patrick's Cathedral. Founded in 1190, St. Patrick's is perhaps best known for its association with Jonathan Swift, who was dean here from 1713 to 1745. Take photos of this impressive structure from the outside. Travel past the Guinness Brewery – home of the famous 'Black Stuff' – to Phoenix Park. Around Europe's largest enclosed public park, you'll see the homes of Ireland's president and the American ambassador. Driving back along the North Bank of the River Liffey, you will pass the Four Courts of Justice and Customs House. The Custom House was designed by James Gandon and completed in 1791. Crossing the Liffey back to Dublin's south side, you will pass the Old Parliament House, now the Bank of Ireland. Watch for Trinity College, founded in 1592 by Queen Elizabeth I, it is Ireland's oldest college. Its library houses the world-famous Book of Kells, a hand-illuminated manuscript of the Gospels. Following this introduction to Dublin City, you will return to Dun Laoghaire and your awaiting ship.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/888014-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDMzMjZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGhrTDJnelpTODRPVEk0TkRJd09UVTBNVFF5THpnNE9EQXhOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wyZjg4MDY3MTAxOGU2MDQ3NWIxODI4MzY2OWYyZTFmOGYxMWY1ODFiM2Y1ZDk4MDk5ZmJkODhiMmY0YjUyZDU0', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '888010', 'port_slug': 'dun-laoghaire-dublin-ireland', 'title': 'River Cruise & City Sights', 'slug': 'river-cruise--city-sights-888010', 'price': 164.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 1.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/888010-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDM1NDV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0ppTDJoaE5DODRPVEk0TkRFNE1qQXhOak13THpnNE9EQXhNQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wzMDUzM2ViN2Q2YzgzZmMwMDdmOWIwZjA0NTRjM2E2ZWM5NWM3YTFkYmMxMDRkYzdjZTRkYzY4Y2U4MjcwOTU0&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
