    {'code': '190043', 'port_slug': 'hilo', 'title': 'VIP Volcanoes National Park and Waterfall', 'slug': 'vip-volcanoes-national-park-and-waterfall-190043', 'price': 284.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 4.5, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/190043-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDMwMjR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFZtTDJnNE9DODRPVEF3TWpJek1UY3lOak00THpFNU1EQTBNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w3MWY5NzYyMWIwMDk0ZmU2YWQyYWM4ZTdjMjkwZjcxYTFhOWY5MGZhM2Q3YTc4ZTViNjUyZTE1MTcwZTc4MzYx', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '190054', 'port_slug': 'hilo', 'title': 'Tropical Farm Tour & Rainbow Falls', 'slug': 'tropical-farm-tour--rainbow-falls-190054', 'price': 169.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/190054-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDYxNTN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFJpTDJnd01pODRPVEF3TWpBNE56ZzNORGcyTHpFNU1EQTFOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w0ZTJiOTFmNmI0ZmY0NDYwZmMyNDE2ZDJiNjJhMzM5YzUwZWMzM2UyNjU0MmM3OTZlZWRhNTExYWY2ZDJlYjNj', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '882002', 'port_slug': 'holyhead', 'title': 'Caernarfon Castle', 'slug': 'caernarfon-castle-882002', 'price': 199.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.5, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': "<p>Your journey to Caernarfon will take you across the island of Anglesey to cross the Menai Straits via the imposing Britannia Bridge, which rises 90 ft. above the channel, supported by piers of Anglesey limestone. The island of Anglesey was the last stronghold of the Druids during the Roman invasion of Britain and later became the refuge of the Welsh princes who resisted the English invasion of the 13th century. Your destination is Caernarfon Village – one of the historic centers of Wales. Its remote past is enshrined in legend for, more than seven hundred years ago, an English king chose it to be the seat of a new administration and gave it newfound fame as the cradle of a line of English princes. The castle and town walls, built at that time and still surviving, were successors to a Roman fortification raised more than a thousand years earlier. Your tour of Caernarfon Castle will reveal one of the most impressive of all the castles built by Edward I. Its majestic walls may well have been modeled on those of Constantinople. Continue to Llanfairpwllgwyngyllgogerychwyrndrobwllllantysiliogogogoch – the local village whose name resembles an unfortunate accident with a can of alphabet soup. This is, in fact, the longest place name in Britain. Take a photo of the sign on the railway platform that bears the village's name (bring a wide-angle lens).</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/882002-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTk2MDl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR015TDJnMU55ODRPVEUyTURVNE56QXhPRFUwTHpnNE1qQXdNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w4M2IwZWQ5YTk5ZjkwNzM3MGVhZGI0OGQ2ZmYxNDYwMTk2ODAzNzQyMWM2MDY4NzJhYWFmZGFiZjM1Yzg0MWQ1', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '882004', 'port_slug': 'holyhead', 'title': 'Countryside Drive & Welsh Tea', 'slug': 'countryside-drive--welsh-tea-882004', 'price': 234.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/882004-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDcyMTR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREF4TDJneVpDODRPVEUyTURZd05UWTVOak13THpnNE1qQXdOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wzZjNkYWZhN2ZmY2YzOGYwYzk2OTVkMWFmNzEwZTBiYTVmMDgwYWJhOTc4ZGM3MTBjNzBkZjkyOTJkN2IzNjIw', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '882008', 'port_slug': 'holyhead', 'title': 'Portmeirion & Llanberis', 'slug': 'portmeirion--llanberis-882008', 'price': 229.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>This is a fantastic panoramic tour around the stunning Snowdonia National Park. This series of dramatic mountain peaks, separated by beautiful valleys, is dotted with pretty towns and villages. We visit the fascinating village of Portmeirion, which will appeal to anyone with an interest in architecture, gardens, and the famous Portmeirion Pottery.</p>\n<p>Departing Holyhead, we travel through the lush countryside of the Isle of Angelsey and across the Menai Straits, a spectacular narrow strip of cascading seawater, separating Isle of Anglesey from Wales. Passing through Caernarfon, with its dramatic 13th century castle, we skirt the Snowdonia National Park and arrive at the picturesque private village of Portmeirion, near the town of Porthmadog.</p>\n<p>Portmeirion was built between 1925 and 1978 by Clough Williams-Ellis, an eccentric architect whose vision was to build an ideal village to enhance, rather than blend into, its surroundings. The result is continually surprising with hidden entrances, distorted perspectives with tantalizing glimpses of the sea or the sands, revealed as you walk through the buildings. Mr. Williams-Ellis’ daughter, Susan, established the famous Portmeirion Pottery in 1960. The “Botanic Garden” series is one of the most popular in the range and features different plants on each piece along with butterflies and other insects and the famous triple leaf motif on the outside.</p>\n<p>Departing Portmeirion, we head inland into the heart of the national park, passing through more wild and rugged scenery and travelling through the Pass of Llanberis in the shadow of Mount Snowdon, the highest of all the peaks in Wales and England. We stop at the village of Llanberis in its delightful lakeside setting, the departure point for the Snowdon Mountain Railway and the easiest way to climb the mountain!</p>\n<p>From Llanberis, the countryside becomes less mountainous as we head back to the coast. Finally, we re-cross the Menai Straits and return to Holyhead.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/882008-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDYyMDl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGRoTDJnMk5DODRPVEl5TXpJd056TXlNVGt3THpnNE1qQXdPQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w3OTU5ZGFmMTJiNmUxZDg1NWJiN2NkZjAzNGY2MTQ5YzRiZDk0MWY5ZjBmYzg2ZjZmM2IyMTIzM2UwZmNkZmJj', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '882006', 'port_slug': 'holyhead', 'title': 'Snowdonia Panoramic', 'slug': 'snowdonia-panoramic-882006', 'price': 224.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 2.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p>This panoramic tour gives you a nice overview of the Welsh countryside and Snowdonia.</p>\n<p>You will begin by first traveling through Anglesey, cross the Menai Strait, and then through Caernarfon with views of its famous castle that dates back to 1283. It was here that the heir to the British throne, Prince Charles, was crowned Prince of Wales in 1969. We continue inland towards the magnificent landscapes of the Snowdonia National Park. This incredible park boasts some of the most amazing scenery to be found anywhere in Wales and is a visual delight.</p>\n<p>As you travel deep into the park, we’ll make a comfort stop at Llanberis, which rests beside the Llyn Padarn Lake. From here, you will take the incredible Llanberis pass that skirts the base of Snowdon, the highest peak in Britain, south of the Scottish Highlands at 3,560 ft. high.</p>\n<p>Drive through the small mountain village of Capel Curig before heading northwest along the A5 Nant Francon Pass back to Holyhead.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/882006-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDIzMjB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGRtTDJneFlTODRPVEl5TXpFNE56WTJNVEV3THpnNE1qQXdOaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xiOTFlNWYyOTRmNGU5NjFmYjIzOTM2MzZmNzdhMTZlNjlkMTQyMWIwYjQ0NGIzOGIwNGNhNjI0YjIxNDk0YTZm', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '882009', 'port_slug': 'holyhead', 'title': 'Fabulous Festinoig Railway and Welsh Countryside', 'slug': 'fabulous-festinoig-railway-and-welsh-countryside-882009', 'price': 269.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/882009-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDM2MjJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGt4TDJobVpDODVNREkzTVRFNU16RTNNREl5THpnNE1qQXdPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w4YThkMmU3YTg3MzI3Mjg5OWQxMzViMjg3OThmMjc3MDM3OTVlZjg1ZjNkMzk2MmU5OTdhNmYzYjIwNjEwYzU2', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '882010', 'port_slug': 'holyhead', 'title': 'Penrhyn Castle', 'slug': 'penrhyn-castle-882010', 'price': 214.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/ComingSoonEurope-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTkzNTl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFF4TDJoak9TODRPVEV4T0RVMk5UQXdOelkyTDBOdmJXbHVaMU52YjI1RmRYSnZjR1V0YVcxbk1TNXFjR2N8OTQwYzM1ZTMxNWE5NmViNjI1N2E5OTNlZWUxNGI4NGU5ZmIyYjg3MDY5ZTNhOWM1NDNjNzQxNzI3M2ZiZDNhMg', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '882005', 'port_slug': 'holyhead', 'title': 'Historic Beaumaris & Castle', 'slug': 'historic-beaumaris--castle-882005', 'price': 229.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p>Explore a 13th-century stronghold of Edward I, then take an independent stroll through an ancient town. You\'ll travel across the island of Anglesey to the enchanting small town of Beaumaris. The nearby Beaumaris Castle is an unfinished masterpiece – a member of the "iron ring" of North Wales castles built by the English monarch Edward I. Beaumaris is nonetheless an awesome sight, regarded by many as the finest of all the great Edwardian castles in Wales, the most perfect in terms of design. The stronghold stands at one end of Castle Street, inextricably linked with the history of the town. This was the beau marais (fair marsh) that Edward chose for a castle and garrison town. Imagine yourself as a 13th-century courtier as you cross the moat via the drawbridge and enter Beaumaris Castle for independent exploration. If you had ever felt you wanted to see a real castle, then Beaumaris is it. The town of Beaumaris, looking out across the Menai Strait to the mountains of Snowdonia on the North Wales mainland, was founded in 1296, after Edward I decided to build the castle here. The town became one of the most important ports in Wales – a center for farming, fishing, seafaring and piracy. During Victorian times, Beaumaris\' economy shifted to tourism as the first steamships brought visitors to the town. A stroll through Beaumaris is a journey through history, complete with medieval fortifications, old inns, elegant Georgian and Victorian townhouses, churches and chapels.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/882005-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDYwNTV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1U1TDJnek9DODRPVEUyTURZeE5ESXhOVGs0THpnNE1qQXdOUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w4YWM0NjFmZTQxODUxYTZiNWNjYzM1NjM5NjIyYzdkZWYxMmIwOGZmN2I3ZTU1MGVmNjBlNmJhZjUyOWJiNTEy', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '882007', 'port_slug': 'holyhead', 'title': 'Beautiful Bodnant Gardens & Snowdonia', 'slug': 'beautiful-bodnant-gardens--snowdonia-882007', 'price': 219.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 1.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/882007-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNDU5MjR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGRtTDJnNE5DODRPVEl5TXpFNU56Z3hPVEU0THpnNE1qQXdOeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w3ODg3ZjFhNGE2NjIxNzQ0N2Q0ZjFmMTVlY2FjMTI5YTczOWMzY2JjYWExMTFkZTM5MGE1NjJmNmEzMDVlOWJm', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '882003', 'port_slug': 'holyhead', 'title': 'Conwy Castle & Shopping', 'slug': 'conwy-castle--shopping-882003', 'price': 239.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': "<p>Despite having been governed from Westminster since 1536, Wales is very much a separate country with its own distinct Celtic identity. It is partly because of the rugged terrain that the Welsh have managed to maintain their separate identity and their ancient language. Your day in North Wales will showcase a bilingual policy where road signs are in both Welsh and English, and you'll be intrigued by the place names made up of native words that describe features of the landscape or ancient buildings. First, travel across Anglesey to the Menai Strait with its wooded banks separating the island from the mainland of North Wales. Make the most of a photo stop at Beaumaris Castle, the eighth and last of the castles built by Edward I to maintain his conquest of North Wales. Today, the castle is the focal point of the elegant little resort town of Beaumaris, with its peaceful streets and graceful yachts moored in the harbor. There are fine coastal views as the main road sweeps along past the resort towns of North Wales towards Conwy, in its setting between the wide estuary and Snowdonia's foothills. Visit Conwy Castle – a masterpiece of medieval architecture. Conwy is one of the most picturesque of Welsh castles, boasting eight beautifully proportioned towers. Explore the castle, walking around the empty ruins, climbing its battlements, and looking down through the floorless towers and roofless rooms. Conwy town is one of the best examples of a medieval walled town in Britain. It is little wonder that Conwy is designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Later, you will stop at Llanfairpwll, the local and abbreviated title for the village boasting the longest name in Britain with 58 letters. You'll have time for shopping at the large Pringle Woolen Store, where you can browse and shop for knitwear, sweaters, clothing, Welsh crafts, gifts and souvenirs.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/882003-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDcwMjl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1V5TDJoaU55ODRPVEUyTURVNU5EVTFOVEU0THpnNE1qQXdNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w4NTYyZjdjZmI5ZWE1ZjdkNDM3ZmQxNmUzNmExZDg4YjJhMjRhZWFlYTY1ZWM3NDJjNmI1NzhhYmJkZmIzZmQz', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '736004', 'port_slug': 'hong-kong', 'title': 'Hong Kong Evening View by Tram', 'slug': 'hong-kong-evening-view-by-tram-736004', 'price': 109.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/736004-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDI4NTV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFE0TDJoa055ODVOVFEzTURFeE1qSTNOamM0THpjek5qQXdOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xkMTY2YTFkZDBkMWRiMmJlMTA4ODJlZDVhZWNkMTM3NDZhOWI0MjIyMjI0OWZmZWQ5YWM5ZTk1NjI0N2M5MWZj', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
