    {'code': '191049', 'port_slug': 'kona', 'title': 'Go Local: Foody Experience by Foot', 'slug': 'go-local--foody-experience-by-foot-191049', 'price': 219.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/191049-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQyMjh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFV6TDJneE1pODRPVEEyTURZNE1qazFOekV3THpFNU1UQTBPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xmYWQ1MTU1NWRjMzMyOWM1NWRmNzRjYTM3YTQyOGMwY2QzZjQxYmJlZjhhNzVjYzVhYmNlYWE1MmJkYjhmOWRj', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '191052', 'port_slug': 'kona', 'title': 'Gold Coast & Cloud Forest Reserve', 'slug': 'gold-coast--cloud-forest-reserve-191052', 'price': 209.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/191052-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTM2Mzd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREF6TDJnNU1DODRPVE0zTURneU9UYzRNek0wTHpFNU1UQTFNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3wxOWNmYjY3NzdlMGNmYjA4MmM5YWMyNzQzNDJmYTA3NWY2YWFmMzVlNTY2NTMzNTY4NjE1ZDBlNzk3YWM4NWZi', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '901006', 'port_slug': 'kotor', 'title': 'Cruising Kotor Bay', 'slug': 'cruising-kotor-bay-901006', 'price': 109.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>A boat ride takes you across Kotor Bay for a magnificent view of the Gospa od Skrpjela Baroque church, set on one of the two islets. According to legend, the islet was made over the centuries by the seamen who kept an ancient oath. Upon returning from each successful voyage, they laid a rock in the bay and, over time, the islet gradually emerged from the sea. The island is just across from the town of Perast, and its church contains 68 magnificent paintings by Tripo Kokolja, a famous 17th-century artist from Perast. His most famous painting, ten yards long, is <em>The Death of the Virgin</em>. Perast is a sleepy Baroque town with beautiful buildings dating back to the 17th and 18th centuries. It is a small and peaceful place, abounding in sacred monuments, including the Church of St. Nicholas built between the 15th and 17th centuries. Here, you will visit the Maritime Museum to learn of Perast’s long and lasting association with the sea.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Cruising-Kotor-Bay-HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyODc3MzN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzVNaTlvTURrdk9EZ3hOREU0TURVNU56YzVNQzVxY0djfDU2MTUxNDliNDJhM2IzNmI2Y2FlYzM0ZWQwNjQ1M2IyODI0NTk3ZWQwMWVkMzc1Y2M5Y2Q3NDc0NTk2NzU1NDI', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '901017', 'port_slug': 'kotor', 'title': 'Montenegro Wild Beauty - Lipa Cave', 'slug': 'montenegro-wild-beauty--lipa-cave-901017', 'price': 109.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p>Explore Montenegro's history, spectacular landscapes, and top highlights on this scenic motorcoach sightseeing tour. Your tour starts from the port, up the mountain road, to the village of Njegusi. Along the way, a stop will be made to admire the view of Boka Bay. Njegusi Village is well known for its national cuisine. Enjoy a snack of smoked ham and cheese, local brandy and wine – all local specialties at this peaceful village. You will continue the trip to Lipa Cave, one of the largest cave monuments in Montenegro. Get ready for a pure adventure in Lipa Cave, which offers a charming diversity of karstic features and provides the visitors with a unique experience of the underground world. After that, go on a panoramic ride down the mountains, enjoying beautiful views of the coast and spectacular scenery before you arrive to Kotor, where you will have an introductory tour of this unique town, a cultural UNESCO World Heritage Site.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/lipa-cave-901017-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNTI0NTB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3hOUzlvTkdFdk9EZ3pNakl4TmpFM01EVXlOaTVxY0djfDM3MjNiNjZkODVmYWFkZWIxZDkyZTQwZTI5ZGI2ODljMTcwNTgzOTU5MDg2NmZjMzViOTI4ZTY4OTA0ZTVkMTk', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '901004', 'port_slug': 'kotor', 'title': 'Budva, Kotor & Coastal Views', 'slug': 'budva-kotor--coastal-views-901004', 'price': 109.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>This excursion showcases the beautiful Montenegrin Riviera, starting with sightseeing in the city of Budva – the center of Montenegrin tourism. Visit the Old Town, tucked safely and secretly inside walls dating from the 15th century. You will have some free time in Budva to enjoy a snack (at your own expense) or shopping. Then, board a motorcoach and drive along the coast to Kotor, enjoying the beautiful view of Kotor Bay. A walking tour takes you through the old medieval Mediterranean town – a UNESCO World Heritage Site – to visit the Cathedral of St. Triphon (12th century) and the Maritime Museum. You will view the Orthodox Church of St. Luka from the outside.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/Budva-Kotor-Coastal-Views-HERO-.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3w0NTMxMzl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGpPUzlvWmpndk9EZ3hPREEwT0RjeU9URXhPQzVxY0djfGY2YTkzMWY2NTg2YTdkMjA2MDhmNmI0OTg1ZWM5ZDFmMDkwNGIwYWRjYzU2MTVlOGFkZDY4MDUyOTViZTNkODU', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '901010', 'port_slug': 'kotor', 'title': 'Budva & Village Life', 'slug': 'budva--village-life-901010', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>From the port, you will drive by coach to Sveti Stefan, located on an island connected to the mainland by a narrow isthmus. Sveti Stefan was once a small town but is now privately owned and is a getaway village for the privileged few. The isthmus itself is quite lovely in that it is flanked by two pink sandy beaches. Take photos from the shoreline above Sveti Stefan. Budva is one of the oldest cities on the Adriatic Sea. It is surrounded by ramparts dating from the 15th century, including a medieval fortification system complete with city gates, defense walls and towers. The ramparts of the citadel, once a powerful military fortress, are cleverly disguised as a stage festival theater in the summertime. Theatrical performances are also held in a smaller arena, between the churches, so that the various saints – St. Mary, St. Sava and St. Trojica – do their part to ensure that a fun time is had by all. With a sense of the atmosphere of the Middle Ages, continue to the Djuric Family farm in the village of Grbalj. Enjoy this beautiful location and the natural environment, meet the farm animals and pick some vegetables from the rich garden. This amazing estate includes the old family church, a beautiful garden, a smokehouse, a small wine cellar and a typical element of old Montenegrin architecture called a ‘guvno’. This is a stone circular building, typically next to a farmhouse, used for processing the corn or grains. In small villages, people meet, socialize and dance in guvnos. On the farm, you will have the opportunity to try delicious local specialties such as smoked ham, cheese and wine. All the food you will taste is homemade from ingredients grown right there on the estate. Return to the ship after this memorable taste of Montenegro.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/Hero.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzNDk2Nzh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzNPQzlvTVdVdk9EZ3pNakl6TmpnM09Ua3dNaTVxY0djfDVhYzJmNzc5NWU0YjBmNmY4MjhkMzg5YjE3M2E4MWM3NWFkYTc2YzUwM2U3ZDg3Mjc0ZjU4MTgxNmM2MTY2Zjc', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '901007', 'port_slug': 'kotor', 'title': 'Montenegro Highlights', 'slug': 'montenegro-highlights-901007', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>Learn about the rich culture, historical heritage and natural beauty of Montenegro as you travel by motorcoach up into the Lovcen serpentine hills. A beautiful view of Kotor Bay and lovely mountain scenery accompany you en route to Njegusi, where you will visit the village smokehouse. Stop for a snack of smoked ham and cheese, local brandy and wine – all local specialties. Then, continue to the city of Cetinje, the former Montenegrin capital, from where the Montenegrin bishops ruled this small country. It is a place rich with cultural and historical monuments, and you will visit the National Museum, once the palace of King Nikola Petrovic I. Then, head down the mountains towards the city of Budva, one of the oldest settlements on the Adriatic coast at more than 2,000 years old. After a panoramic stop above Budva, you will drive back to Kotor to explore the city that is known as the jewel of Montenegro. Your guide will take you on a walking tour that will include a visit to St. Triphon’s Cathedral and you will view the Orthodox Church of St. Luka from the outside.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Montenegro-Highlights-HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzNDAyMTJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3paQzlvT1Rrdk9EZ3hOREU0TURreU5UUTNNQzVxY0djfDdkNWZjMWUxYmRlYTkxNGQ2NmI3YzE1ZjhhZTU5NDVkNTEyMGEwZTE1ZTkxN2YwZjI2YTJjNjllNzJkOGE2ZjU', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '901008', 'port_slug': 'kotor', 'title': 'Skadar Lake', 'slug': 'skadar-lake-901008', 'price': 169.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/y01-Skadar-Lake-HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyODA3MTd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaG1NaTlvTUdRdk9EZ3hOREU0TVRJeU1ETTRNaTVxY0djfDM5NGRiMzg3YjRhMmRmNzZmNTUwYzg5NmI2MmEwMmNiYjY3NjY3ODMyMWQ1ZTdiOTU4ZDcwMDU1MjAwMDdlZWM', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
