    {'code': '864001', 'port_slug': 'liverpool', 'title': "The Story of Britain's Most Famous Band", 'slug': 'the-story-of-britain-s-most-famous-band-864001', 'price': 174.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<strong>Fab Four:</strong> Step into an immersive multimedia journey at The Beatles Story Museum and trace the Fab Four’s rise from Liverpool roots to worldwide fame.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Strawberry Fields:</strong> Visit Strawberry Field’s famous red gates and peaceful gardens, the inspiring setting behind the classic “Strawberry Fields Forever.”\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Penny Lane:</strong> Enjoy a photo stop at the iconic Penny Lane, a must-see Liverpool landmark tied to the band.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Making the Band:</strong> See the childhood homes, schools, and local venues that helped shape the group’s remarkable story.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Music Marvels:</strong> Continue your musical journey through Liverpool with a guided panoramic drive featuring commentary and views of its famous music and cultural landmarks.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Guided panoramic tour of Liverpool.</li>\n\t<li>Entrance to The Beatles Story Museum.</li>\n\t<li>Visit to Strawberry Field Gardens.</li>\n\t<li>Photo stop at Penny Lane.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/864001-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDY2NjV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRE5sTDJnNFl5ODRPVEk1TXpZeE1UWTJNelkyTHpnMk5EQXdNUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xlZDUwMzhjMmIwM2IxNDA2ZWJkOGMyZDAzN2QyYTk4M2I0ZDQzMmE1MzA3NDdmMjhkMGI3MzhlNzRiY2FmOTk4', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '864002', 'port_slug': 'liverpool', 'title': 'North Wales & Conwy Castle', 'slug': 'north-wales--conwy-castle-864002', 'price': 254.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Scenic Journeys:</strong> Journey through the untouched beauty of North Wales passing serene hills and river valleys, the historic city of Liverpool, the cultural-rich peninsula of The Wirral, and Mold, as well as a scenic route towards the impressive Clwydian range. Encounter the picturesque town of Ruthin, nestled within the stunning Vale of Clwyd, with road and street signs in both English and Welsh.&nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Conwy Castle:</strong> Discover the grandeur of Conwy Castle and its stunning walled town, a true gem of medieval architecture. Stroll along the ancient walls, lined with 21 towers and three gateways, and admire the intricate design of the eight massive towers embedded in the foundation rock, showcasing the masterful craftsmanship of Edward I and his architect, James of St. George.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Independent Explorations:</strong> Experience the charming town of Betws-y-Coed, surrounded by hill country averaging 1,000 feet in altitude. Embrace the enchanting atmosphere enhanced by the River Conwy and three tributaries and use your free time to stroll through craft and gift shops or find a serene spot for lunch on your own before venturing down the Conwy valley.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/864002-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDc0NzV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0pqTDJneU5DODVOalExT0RBeE1qQTVPRGcyTHpnMk5EQXdNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xiMDY0ZWE0YThkNjA5MTJkMTA0M2M3NWE5ZTZkZDk2YThiNTE2ZGRmNzViOTExNTE0NTUxMjViNzE3MjZiMzY4', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '864003', 'port_slug': 'liverpool', 'title': 'A Taste of Chester', 'slug': 'a-taste-of-chester-864003', 'price': 189.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p>Visiting Chester is like taking a magical journey back in time with so much of the past in the streets, in the buildings, and in the air. Chester was originally settled by the Romans as Fortress Deva, named after the River Dee, in the first century AD. With its imposing walls, the original Roman structure still evident in parts today, Deva swiftly became a major garrison during the Roman occupation of Britain.</p>\n<p>By the 1700s, the walls, no longer needed for defense, were styled into the leisurely promenade you know today. One of the most historic settings in Britain, this ravishing little city now guards an awe-inspiring legacy of 2,000 years of British heritage.</p>\n<p>You will drive directly from Liverpool, and on arrival commence a panoramic sightseeing tour along the parts of the city accessible to motor coaches. A visit is then made to the Cathedral. Towering above all other buildings, it was originally a 10th century church, becoming a Cathedral after the dissolution of monasteries by Henry VIII. Full of interest, its 14th century carved choir stalls and monastic buildings are among the finest in the country. The composer Handel gave his first public performance of The Messiah here in 1742.</p>\n<p>The tour then allows for you to be at leisure to visit other parts of Chester on your own. You may care to walk along part of the city’s walls, from where fine elevated views are obtained. Studded with historic towers and ancient gates in the form of imposing arches, the walls offer a bird’s eye view of the city centre on one side with magnificent views of the distant Welsh mountains on the other.</p>\n<p>Not to be missed, and a magnet to every visitor are Chester’s unique half-timbered galleried shops on two levels, the foundations of which are 13th century. Then there is the pretty Victorian Eastgate Clock, the most photographed timepiece in the world after Big Ben. You will see many examples of the black and white architecture - nowhere in Britain is there more - giving Chester its outstanding medieval look.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/864003-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyODI0OTB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREUwTDJnM1l5ODRPVEkyT0RnME5ESTVPRFUwTHpnMk5EQXdNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w3YzRmZTlkMTJhZjdiZjdhNDczMTE0MjYzNjExYjU1ZjRjODc5OTczNWVlN2YxODRhYzk5ZDM5ZmIxYzQyNmMy', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '864011', 'port_slug': 'liverpool', 'title': 'City of Liverpool Walk Tour', 'slug': 'city-of-liverpool-walk-tour-864011', 'price': 129.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p>Starting at the quayside itself, we come immediately to the so-called Three Graces adorning Liverpool’s historic waterfront: The Royal Liver Building, 1911, that would not look out of place in Manhattan, the Italian palatial style Cunard Building, 1917, and the neo-baroque Port of Liverpool Building, 1917, form a formidable waterfront trio, recalling an age of pre-first world war confidence and optimism. On the Liver Building, look out for the twin Liver Birds – the city’s guardian angels. Ornate sculptures adorn the Cunard, and the Port Building’s sheer opulence is a sight to behold.</p>\n<p>Moving south along the waterfront, the daring lines and curves of the Museum of Liverpool remind us that we live in very different times today.</p>\n<p>Behind the Museum of Liverpool, the bold but elegant steel and glass of Mann Island’s Longitude and Latitude buildings complete the contrast with a century earlier.</p>\n<p>In its heyday, Albert Dock’s innovation was to enable ships to berth right alongside warehouses. Built in 1846, its pioneering iron, brick and stone construction involved no wooden framework. Later, a cargo store, today comprehensively renovated, it boasts an excellent selection of hotels, bars, and restaurants.</p>\n<p>Heading up into the city, we pass by the Beaux Arts style Queen Victoria Monument at Derby Square, built on the former site of Liverpool Castle. From here, it is on to Matthew Street and the world-famous Cavern Club, one time haunt of house band, The Beatles.</p>\n<p>The city center contains many buildings of architectural note, reflecting different stages in Liverpool’s trading history. Amongst these, we will pass by the former Adelphi Bank building, 1892, with its stripes of red and grey sandstone, onion domes, and bronze doors; the imposing Town Hall, 1754; Oriel Chambers, 1864, with its ground-breaking metal framed glass curtain wall; the Unity Liverpool office block at 20 Chapel Street, 2006.</p>\n<p>Before returning to the ship, the 19th century Church of Our Lady and Saint Nicholas, damaged in and renovated after the Second World War, serves as a poignant reminder of Liverpool’s past.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/864011-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDI1MTR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGs0TDJnMk1pODRPVEkyT0RjNE5qWXlOamcyTHpnMk5EQXhNUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xlYWJjYjgxOGVjOWYxMDY1NDdiOWJiNWEzNzcyZTE4YThkNDY3ZWRiZDU4OTE1ZTQ3ZjBjNzM0ZTdjYzMyYjQy', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '864013', 'port_slug': 'liverpool', 'title': 'Chester Half Day', 'slug': 'chester-half-day-864013', 'price': 179.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p>On arrival to Chester, you will commence a panoramic sightseeing tour along the parts of the city accessible to motor coaches. Take photographs of Chester Cathedral while your guide explains how a 10th century church became Cathedral Henry VIII. You will then visit the cathedral at your leisure or enjoy other parts of Chester on your own. You may care to walk along part of the city walls, from where fine elevated views are obtained. Return by coach to Liverpool and, if time permits, see some sights on the way back to the pier.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/864013-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQ2Nzl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFF6TDJnd1lpODRPVEkyT0RnMU5qUXlNamN3THpnMk5EQXhNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xkOWRmNDY4YmY2ZGZkZTE2N2U3NjI2YTQzNWZlNmI1YWJiOTM1Y2UyODlkZmIxMzYwYTE1ODE5OWVhMWI0YjVl', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '864004', 'port_slug': 'liverpool', 'title': 'Liverpool City Panoramic', 'slug': 'liverpool-city-panoramic-864004', 'price': 164.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/860004-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDc3NDR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRE00TDJnMU1TODRPVEkyT0RjNE1UTTRNems0THpnMk1EQXdOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w5YmY5MmVjZDY5MDE3N2Y5NWE3YjY2NmQ5MzYxYTQ2MmViNDM2NmE3NmZjZmRkNWE4Zjk5NmM5MmVkNTBlMWM5', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '864010', 'port_slug': 'liverpool', 'title': 'Liverpool & Port Sunlight Panoramic', 'slug': 'liverpool--port-sunlight-panoramic-864010', 'price': 164.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/864010-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDUwMjZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFJoTDJneFppODRPVEkyT0RnMU1EZzFNakUwTHpnMk5EQXhNQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xhMmExNDc4NmY5MzU4NjEzYTVlMWRiYWYwMmVhZWMyZGYzOWJhNWE1ZWM3NTZjODIyMGYzNWI3ZjVkNjVjZjVi', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '812113', 'port_slug': 'livorno-florence-pisa', 'title': 'A Tuscan Day in Volterra & San Gimignano Towns', 'slug': 'a-tuscan-day-in-volterra--san-gimignano-towns-812113', 'price': 169.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.9, 'review_count': 13, 'desc_html': "Enjoy the breathtaking Tuscan countryside with visits to the magnificent towns of San Gimignano and Volterra. Your motor coach will take you on your scenic journey to San Gimignano, recently the landmark for the highly successful movie 'Under the Tuscan Sun'.&nbsp; <p>Explore this beautiful town independently, viewing the &nbsp;Manhattan of Tuscany &nbsp;skyline, with a large number of towers dating back to the 11th and 13th centuries. Enjoy a typical local meal in a nearby farmhouse before heading off to beautiful Volterra, one of the finest, and lesser known, hilltop towns tucked away in the heart of Tuscany.&nbsp;</p> <p>Visit with your guide the famous Piazza Dei Priori and get a close up of the medieval walls, the amphitheater and renaissance palaces. Free time will be given in both towns.&nbsp;</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Beautiful-Tuscany-10.JPG?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzNTM1MTU2fGltYWdlL2pwZWd8YVcxaFoyVnpMMmhsWWk5b1pXTXZPRGd4TWpVMU9ETXhPVFkwTmk1cWNHY3w4ZDc0NmI5ZDQzODI4MjNjNmQ0MzE2MzgxMWNiZTk4YjY5YjNiZGUwZDM3YzgyMDI3OWYxZjdjYzU4NjYxZWQ5', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '812119', 'port_slug': 'livorno-florence-pisa', 'title': 'Cinque Terre & Portovenere Exploration', 'slug': 'cinque-terre--portovenere-exploration-812119', 'price': 204.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.3, 'review_count': 6, 'desc_html': 'Start your tour with a scenic drive to Portovenere, a famous picturesque village which is also A UNESCO World Heritage site. This part of the area of coastline and the surrounding hillsides are already &nbsp;the Cinque Terre National Park.&nbsp; <p><br /> </p> <p>In Portovenere enjoy a guided tour of the village with the visit of the church of St. Peter where the temple of Venus once stood, giving rise to the name Porto Venere. After the guided visit of the village you will enjoy free time for shopping in this lovely place. Then, board a motorboat for a scenic ride along the Cinque Terre: While cruising and admiring the amazing landscape, enjoy a guided commentary. Your boat ride will end at the most famous of the five villages in Cinque Terre, Monterosso al mare.&nbsp;</p> <p>After the guide&rsquo;s introduction, you will have a complimentary pesto tasting at one of the local venues before your approximately 90 minutes of free time to explore the village typical shops, the characteristic historical centre or the inviting restaurants. At the end of your free time you&rsquo;ll take a local train to Levanto (a close-by village) to re-join the coach for your return to the ship.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Cinque-Terre-11.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3w0OTk5NjN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzNaUzlvTjJVdk9EZ3hNalUxT1RNek5UUTFOQzVxY0djfGE1MWUwYjBjNzIxYjRlYmMxMGUzZTBmMmRhYzgwOWNiMDQ2ODk0MTNkODYyYjAzODRlMjg5N2ViMGMzZWUxZDY', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '812111', 'port_slug': 'livorno-florence-pisa', 'title': 'Best of Florence& Michelangelo Masterpiece w/Lunch', 'slug': 'best-of-florence-michelangelo-masterpiece-w-lunch-812111', 'price': 199.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 3, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Divine Architecture:</strong> Journey to Florence, a city brimming with history and architectural wonders. Your walking tour kicks off at the renowned Cathedral of Santa Maria del Fiore, where you'll also see the Baptistery and Campanile Bell Tower.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Piazza Stroll:</strong> Explore the rich history of Florence as you stroll past Piazza della Signoria and Piazza Santa Croce, taking in the stunning exterior of the city’s renowned church.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Picture Perfect:</strong> Capture a moment at the iconic Ponte Vecchio Bridge, a 14th-century architectural gem that offers a perfect backdrop for your Florence adventure.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Accademia:</strong> Visit the renowned Accademia Gallery to witness Michelangelo's magnificent David and explore an impressive array of artistic masterpieces.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Independent Explorations:</strong> Take some time to explore at your leisure and savor a delicious lunch at a traditional Italian restaurant.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Headphones.</li>\n\t<li>Lunch.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Best-of-Florence-14.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyMDAxNzIwfGltYWdlL2pwZWd8YVcxaFoyVnpMMmc1TlM5b1pUa3ZPRGd4TWpVMU56UXdNakUwTWk1cWNHY3wzYzY5NGE3MGZmZTkxYWIzMjE5YjEzOTBlY2FkMmMwZWI0ZGZlYTQ5OTk1MTI3ZGMwZTdmNDNmNjc3ZTg4MTU0', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '812135', 'port_slug': 'livorno-florence-pisa', 'title': 'Small Group: 3 Cinque Terre Villages', 'slug': 'small-group-3-cinque-terre-villages-812135', 'price': 269.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Fishing Villages:</strong> Start your journey as you are brought to La Spezia by motor coach. Once there, you’ll hop on an exclusive and comfortable minibus, the only vehicle allowed in the small villages. Enjoy an exclusive visit to the fishing villages of Riomaggiore and Manarola, appreciating their characteristic landscapes and colors.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Local Flavors:</strong> Next, visit Monterosso al Mare, the area’s oldest and most famous village. While there, sample a selection of local pesto bruschetta, and wine, the crown culinary jewel of this region. You’ll then have some time to explore and shop on your own before being transported back to port via train and motor coach.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Motor coach transfer.</li>\n\t<li>Bruschetta sampler.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/cinque-terre-riomaggiore-manarola-and-monterosso-812135-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTQ2ODR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGtOQzlvWWpRdk9EZ3pNemMwTXpNMU5Ua3pOQzVxY0djfDNkMjViNWRhOWZmOTcwYjQ0NWFmMWRmOTNlYTNkYmI1MDQxZjA3MjllM2RkMTI1YjZlN2NkMDMyNjE1NjNlNDQ', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '812136', 'port_slug': 'livorno-florence-pisa', 'title': 'Tuscany Farm to Table and Wine Tasting', 'slug': 'tuscany-farm-to-table-and-wine-tasting-812136', 'price': 169.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Farm Experience:</strong> Discover the charm of a family-owned estate as you arrive and embark on a horse carriage ride, taking in the picturesque views of the truffle plantation, olive trees, and cultivated vegetables on your way to the farmhouse. Indulge in an organic Tuscan feast featuring fresh vegetables, homemade pastas, accompanied by a generous wine tasting that includes the delightful Vin Santo and delicious Cantuccini biscuits. Take a moment to savor the countryside scenery and engage with the friendly farmers before bidding farewell and returning to the ship.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Tuscan lunch.</li>\n\t<li>Trolley transportation.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/812136-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQ1OTR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREExTDJnME5pODVOalExT0RBeU1qa3hNak13THpneE1qRXpOaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w3M2FlYmJiY2JlMzY1N2Q5NWEyZWE5OGVjN2RmYjM0ZTEwZDY3M2QyNDg5NzdmMGE2MGMyMThmNzgzOTgwMzNk', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
