    {'code': '812121', 'port_slug': 'livorno-florence-pisa', 'title': 'Florence & Pisa with Tower Entrance', 'slug': 'florence--pisa-with-tower-entrance-812121', 'price': 279.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.4, 'review_count': 5, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Florence-and-Pisa-with-Tower-Entrance-15.JPG?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3w0MDkwNTY1fGltYWdlL2pwZWd8YVcxaFoyVnpMMmczWXk5b00yRXZPRGd4TkRJeU1ERXhOVGs1T0M1cWNHY3wxZTEzYjMzZjI1ZGExZmU1NmEwZjBjMGYzOWRkMjg5N2FmNDAyMDhmZmMzMmY2NWI2N2I2NjVjZTQ0NjMzMmZi&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '812120', 'port_slug': 'livorno-florence-pisa', 'title': 'Florence on Your Own', 'slug': 'florence-on-your-own-812120', 'price': 119.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.3, 'review_count': 12, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Florence-on-Your-Own-15.JPG?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNTY1NTR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3hPUzlvTkRndk9EZ3hOREl4T1RneU1UQTROaTVxY0djfDVhOTA2YzYyODc1YzY1NmMyMGQ1ZDIwMjQ4NjA0ZDNiZjY2NTdkNTY5MTQ2Y2E5YjY3MDE0OTViMDYyNDlkNDA&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '354005', 'port_slug': 'maceio', 'title': 'Hibiscus Beach Club Experience', 'slug': 'hibiscus-beach-club-experience-354005', 'price': 129.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Scenic Drive:</strong> Enjoy a scenic drive of about one-hour and fifteen-minutes starting from Maceió to Hibiscus Beach Club. Relax and soak up the views as you make your way to this stunning beach location.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Hibiscus Beach Club:</strong> Retreat to Hibiscus Beach Club situated by the serene Ipioca shoreline. Relax on shaded loungers, sip refreshing cocktails, and bask in the sun on golden sands. Enjoy live music and luxurious beachside vibes for an unforgettable experience.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Hibiscus Restaurant:</strong> Treat yourself to a vibrant array of coastal cuisine featuring grilled seafood and shrimp risotto. Dine al fresco beneath thatched roofs and enjoy stunning ocean views with each bite. Please be aware that this dining experience is available at an extra cost.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>One bottle of water per person.</li>\n\t<li>Beach chairs and umbrella.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/354005-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyODQ1NTV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREF4TDJnM09TODVNVE16TkRNMk5EWTVNamM0THpNMU5EQXdOUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w1ODE2ODRjNmQ3OGU5YjlkYmE3YzdhMjdiMDVmMzhiNTVjZjZmMTJhNDY1MmMyYTM1NWUwNjFiYjdhZTIwNjUw', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '354002', 'port_slug': 'maceio', 'title': 'Maceio & Marechal Deodoro with Beach Lunch', 'slug': 'maceio--marechal-deodoro-with-beach-lunch-354002', 'price': 144.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<strong>Scenic Maceio:</strong> Experience the picturesque shoreline of Maceio as you pass Pajucara, Ponta Verde, and Jatiuca. Enjoy the colorful jangadas and notable sights like the Church of Martirios, City Hall and Deodoro Theater. Conclude your tour with panoramic views from Mirante de Sao Goncalo.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Colonial Charm:</strong> Discover the history of Marechal Deodoro, once the capital of Alagoas and the birthplace of Brazil's first president. Enjoy the beauty of the Church of Santa Maria Madalena and the intriguing façades of local museums. Meander through the cobblestone streets and experience the charm of this colonial gem.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Beach Break:</strong> Unwind at Praia do Frances, a beloved Brazilian beach known for its laid-back vibe. Swim in the stunning emerald waters or enjoy a meal at a beach bar featuring fresh local seafood and regional favorites.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Marechal Deodoro:</strong> Venture to Marechal Deodoro, a picturesque town with deep historical roots. Stroll through the local craft market where you can admire handmade lace, embroidery, and authentic keepsakes celebrating the artisan culture of Alagoas.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong>\n<ul>\n    <li>Lunch at Olibaba Beach Kiosk: Guests can choose one starter, main course, dessert – shrimp soup, bean soup, house style picanha, fish moqueca, seafood risotto, pudding, passion fruit moose.</li>\n    <li>Beach chairs & umbrella.</li>\n    <li>One coconut water per person.</li>\n    <li>One bottle of water per person.</li>\n</ul>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/354002-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDYzNjl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGcwTDJnNU15ODVNVE16TWpNNU5qazNORE00THpNMU5EQXdNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w2ZmUyZmRiNDFjM2RmNDMwNzAwOGZlMGFmMTA3ZDg4NGIwYjc5NWNjYjMyNDk4ZGJhOGIwMGVlNjlkMTMyZTk3', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '354004', 'port_slug': 'maceio', 'title': 'Islands & Lagoons of Maceio', 'slug': 'islands--lagoons-of-maceio-354004', 'price': 139.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Pontal da Barra:</strong> Depart from the port by coach to the picturesque fishing village of Pontal da Barra located just south of the city. Enjoy a scenic cruise on a traditional boat across one of Brazil's largest and most diverse lagoon systems.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Mundau Lagoon:</strong> Sail through the tranquil waters of Lagoa do Mundaú, exploring nine captivating islands and dense mangrove forests. Marvel at the pristine beaches and observe local fishermen going about their daily routines for a taste of genuine coastal life.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Prainha Lagoon:</strong> Relax at Prainha Lagoon, where crystal-clear waters await you for a refreshing swim. Surrounded by vibrant tropical landscapes and bright sunlight, it provides an ideal setting to rejuvenate and enjoy nature.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>One bottle of water per person.</li>\n\t<li>Beach chairs and umbrella.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/354004-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDcwODV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGM1TDJneE5TODVNVE16TkRNMU5qRTNNekV3THpNMU5EQXdOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wxYjg3ZTBjYWVmZDFlM2NjODE5MGE4NTNiMTE1ZmFiMDU1NWVmYTI5NDFjOWFjNjAzNjEyZWZiYzcwNzg1NWE4', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '354003', 'port_slug': 'maceio', 'title': 'Meet Maceio: Culture, Crafts & Praia do Frances', 'slug': 'meet-maceio-culture-crafts--praia-do-frances-354003', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>City Highlights:</strong> Embark on a scenic drive through Maceió's Jaraguá District, where colorful colonial and baroque architecture reveal the city's past. Along the way, you will see important cultural sites like Martírios Church, City Hall, and the Deodoro Theater.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Local Treasures:</strong> Head to Pontal da Barra, a colorful handicraft district celebrated for its intricate lace and embroidery. Spend time browsing the artisan shops and selecting authentic souvenirs.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Lagoon Views:</strong> Take a southward journey along Maceió’s beautiful shoreline, admiring the serene Lagoa do Mundaú and Lagoa Manguaba. These lagoons are integral to one of Brazil's most captivating ecosystems.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Beach Break:</strong> Unwind at Praia do Frances, a beloved Brazilian beach known for its laid-back vibe. Swim in the stunning emerald waters or treat yourself to a meal at a beach bar featuring fresh local seafood and regional favorites.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>One coconut water per person.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/354003-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQzOTF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREl5TDJnMlppODVNVE16TWpRd01EVTNPRGcyTHpNMU5EQXdNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w0YjdmODI5NzEyMzQ4MDEyNzAwMTA4YjRjMGNjZGQ2MDhiZmYwOTVhNzc1ZTlhMTAzNWMwMGZkNmQ0YTcyYzMw', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '813061', 'port_slug': 'malaga', 'title': 'Charming Malaga & Flamenco', 'slug': 'charming-malaga--flamenco-813061', 'price': 129.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.5, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': "Discover Malaga's rich archaeological remains and fascinating monuments on this panoramic drive past its marvelous landmarks. Ancient history is alive and well in this busy center of the Costa del Sol, and civilizations old and older have left remnants for you to admire and ponder. View from the outside, the stunning architecture of the Alcazaba Palace, built in the 11th century for the Arabian Caliphs. Next, a glimpse of the Renaissance-style cathedral awaits you. It was built between the 16th and 18th centuries and now is a national monument. During your drive, you will also see the façade of the bullring (one of the busiest in Spain), and some interesting and beautiful buildings from the 19th century, including City Hall, the Justice Court and the Central Post Office. Then, enjoy free time, shopping in the Old Quarter, especially in Larios Street, the most famous shopping street in the area. Finally, you will experience an extraordinary and authentic flamenco show, where you will discover all the keys to understand this musical style full of passion and emotion, which is, without a doubt, one of the icons of Spanish culture. It is provocative, fun and sensual—full of gestures, touches, looks, and movement that have no script. UNESCO decided to include flamenco on the Representative List of the Intangible Cultural World Heritage, which is the greatest international distinction for any cultural expression. After the show, venture into the city by bus to explore the beauty of Malaga, take in the sights such as Picasso´s birthplace, Fuente de las Tres Gracias, Merced Square and the exterior of Malaga´s famous Cathedral with an expert guide.", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-813061-Charming-Malaga-Flamenco-Cathedral-212.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMjIzNDl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3pOUzlvTW1Rdk9EZ3hNemc1TWpnMk1UazRNaTVxY0djfDQzYWM5MWY3MGEyY2I3NDViN2Y5YWYyNGMxMDNjM2NjMDYwYzYxYjY1NDc2ZTI3OGY3ZmNkZDg1ZGM5OGIxZGM', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '813063', 'port_slug': 'malaga', 'title': 'Malaga Sights & Picasso Museum', 'slug': 'malaga-sights--picasso-museum-813063', 'price': 119.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.3, 'review_count': 3, 'desc_html': "<p>If you take delight in ancient history, you won’t want to miss this tour. With half a million inhabitants, Malaga is the major coastal city of Andalusia and is a genuinely traditional city of this province. Its gritty individualism remains untouched by tourism and, to a large extent, the passage of time. Many ancient civilizations have left their mark, which you’ll discover in Malaga’s rich archaeological remains and fascinating monuments. On your way to Gibralfaro Castle, pass by the Alcazaba – a historic palace that was built in the 11th century to be the residence of the Arabian Caliphs (kings). It is connected by a steep path to the Gibralfaro Castle – an ancient Moorish fortress which commands breathtaking views of the city and the bay. The Museo Picasso Malaga is run by two foundations created for the purpose of showcasing the works of the master. The Fundación Paul, Christine y Bernard Ruiz-Picasso owns the museum’s collection, whereas the Fundación Museo Picasso de Malaga owns the group of buildings that house it. Together, the two foundations are responsible for the conservation, exhibition, study and diffusion of the art, and that the wishes of the donors are respected. At the museum, you will have time to appreciate all of Picasso's styles and techniques (painting, drawing, sculpture, ceramic and graphic works) along with an exhibition with pieces dating from 1890 to 1973.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/813063-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDI0NjF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGRoTDJobE55ODRPVFl3TWpZeE5ESXpNVE0wTHpneE16QTJNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w2M2FjMzYxZGFkN2IyMThhNWM0YjVjMWU0OWQ0MzNmMThiMDk2MDNhZWEyZjY1ZDNiNzMwOWU2OTdhZDYzMGY1', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '813062', 'port_slug': 'malaga', 'title': 'Marbella & Puerto Banus', 'slug': 'marbella--puerto-banus-813062', 'price': 104.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 1.5, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': "This tour begins with a panoramic view of Malaga, before continuing the 45-minute journey to Marbella, the pearl of the Costa del Sol and one of the most important holiday destinations for international tourism. Here, you'll discover the beauty of its historic center with its typical Andalusian charm and ambience. Admire the white houses with balconies full of flowers, and small winding roads filled with restaurants, bars and shops. From there, the tour will head to Puerto Banus, a tourist resort near Marbella. There will be plenty of time to enjoy the marina, which is also renowned for its exciting nightlife.", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-813062MarbellaPuertoBus2.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3w1MDMzMzZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3paQzlvTnpBdk9EZ3hNemc1TXpRNE5EVTNOQzVxY0djfDM0OWNkM2NhYmRiZGFmMjg1MDM1NmNkOWM3N2I5NWRhMmRiNDU0NDkwMTEwNzdiM2Y3MjlmNzhiMzE4OTBjODI', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '813056', 'port_slug': 'malaga', 'title': 'The Best of Malaga', 'slug': 'the-best-of-malaga-813056', 'price': 109.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 1.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p>A cocktail of highlights featuring the best of Malaga’s sights. A photo stop will be made to take in the magnificent panoramic views over the city, so don’t forget your camera. A visit will be made to the Arabic Fortress of Alcazaba, perched high upon the hillside of the Gibralfaro Mountain, where fine views of the African coastline can be enjoyed. Your guide will highlight how the Andalusian culture is ever-present within the Fortress, with its many fountains, channels and ponds. At the foot of this ancient Fortress, you can also view the excavated ruins of a Roman amphitheater. The tour continues with a walk to the birthplace and home of the 20th century’s most popular and contemporary artist – Pablo Picasso. Passing through the rooms of his house, your guide will bring to life Picasso’s early years and explain that, even as a toddler, Picasso began to draw his surroundings, which included pigeons and, bizarrely, Churros – a dough type pastry. Leaving the birthplace of Picasso, enter the typical traditional bodega of El Pimpi, where a glass of sherry and some olives will be served.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-813056-The-Best-of-Malaga-Alcazaba-Malaga-53.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzNDIzODh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGtOeTlvTVRrdk9EZ3hNemc1TVRVNE5EQXpNQzVxY0djfGM0YjhiNWZkMGIwZWNlZDc5YTRmZDk5MjY5MTEwNTE5MTcwZWZmNTA5MGYxMDM5MmIzY2EyODc0OGNlZTA1YWI', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '813084', 'port_slug': 'malaga', 'title': 'CAMINITO DEL REY: A DIVE INTO THE NATURE', 'slug': 'caminito-del-rey-a-dive-into-the-nature-813084', 'price': 119.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Caminito del Rey:</strong> Take a walk across the heart of Desfiladero de los Gaitanes, a ravine known for its breathtaking beauty. The trail is suspended one hundred meters above the ground, providing vertiginous views of the surrounding landscapes that were once exclusive to experienced climbers. The elevation offers stunning and dramatic views of the exceptional natural environment. During the nature walk, learn about the local fauna, explore the unique flora, and discover the geological features that contribute to the charm of the surroundings. This educational component adds depth to your nature walk, providing a holistic understanding of the ecosystem.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/813084-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDkyNTl8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREF6TDJnMFlpODVNREV6TVRnMU56QTRNRFl5THpneE16QTROQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xjYTNkZjZkZWYwNDA5OTBjMTkzNDE1NGY3MjkwOWVjNjQ1ZjhkMDIxNGQ3YWQ1YzYyZGZlYTdiYjgwZDJmMDI3', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
