    {'code': '319042', 'port_slug': 'manzanillo', 'title': 'Manzanillo Makers: Crystals, Clay & Countryside', 'slug': 'manzanillo-makers-crystals-clay--countryside-319042', 'price': 84.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/319042-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTYxNjV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0kwTDJnNU5TODVOVGd3TnpRd01qZ3dNelV3THpNeE9UQTBNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xiYWE4OThhNTAwNzllNWJmODUzNjkxZTk0ZDI1NTg2MGUwNjE1ZWYwZWI4MTdmOTQ3YTIzZDQ5MWQxMDZhNThi', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '319037', 'port_slug': 'manzanillo', 'title': 'Manzanillo: City Sights, Bites & Shopping', 'slug': 'manzanillo-city-sights-bites--shopping-319037', 'price': 42.5, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/319037-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNzQyMjd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFUyTDJnd1pDODVOVFl3TnpjNE5qY3dNVEV3THpNeE9UQXpOeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3wyNTc1OTY1MmMyNTBmZjA5NTI0MTQ3MGViZDNiNDcwN2E2MmE3MTg1MWE0ZmZhY2VhOTQzNTU2ZmNhOTA5ODFh', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '820039', 'port_slug': 'marseilles-provence', 'title': "Provence's Hilltop Villages: Roussillon & Gordes", 'slug': 'provence-s-hilltop-villages-roussillon--gordes-820039', 'price': 139.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Roussillon Views:</strong> Explore colorful Roussillon, one of France’s most picturesque villages, where dramatic red, orange and gold ochre cliffs contrast beautifully with the surrounding Provençal countryside.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Ochre Discovery:</strong> Discover the area’s famous ochre formations and see how their vivid natural pigments helped define the landscape, architecture and artistic heritage of the region.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Independent Explorations:</strong> Spend time at leisure in Roussillon, with opportunities to shop local boutiques, take in scenic viewpoints and enjoy lunch in this picturesque Provençal village.&nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Hilltop Village::</strong> Visit Gordes, one of France’s most beautiful villages, dramatically perched above the Imergue Valley with stone houses cascading down the hillside, cobblestone lanes, historic archways and picturesque squares. &nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Countryside Drive:</strong> Enjoy a scenic drive through rolling vineyards, lavender fields and breathtaking Provençal landscapes long admired by artists and travelers alike.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>A visit to Roussillon with guided orientation and free time.</li>\n\t<li>Visit the ochre quarries and viewpoints.</li>\n\t<li>A visit to Gordes with guided orientation and free time.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/820039-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDY0OTV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFZpTDJnMFppODVOakUzTWpBeU5UYzNORE00THpneU1EQXpPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w2OGQzYTgyNTVkMjU2ZGQ4MDhmYWJiMTA0ZjIyYWQyYzIxNzg3Y2ZiZjU1OTA5NjBmNzE1MDU0MjRmZmQ1ZWM1', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '820043', 'port_slug': 'marseilles-provence', 'title': 'Aix En Provence City Stroll', 'slug': 'aix-en-provence-city-stroll-820043', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Capital Charm:</strong> Visit Aix-en-Provence, Provence’s capital, celebrated for graceful architecture, lively streets, tree-lined boulevards, historic squares and its famed “City of a Thousand Fountains” charm, showcased in beautiful water features found throughout the city. &nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Avenue Stroll:</strong> Stroll Cours Mirabeau, Aix’s most famous avenue, lined with grand mansions, fountains, cafés and centuries of Provençal history. &nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Mazarin Quarter:</strong> Discover the Mazarin Quarter, one of France’s finest examples of 17th-century urban planning, with elegant residences, picturesque squares and historic streets.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Saint-Sauveur Cathedral:</strong> Admire Saint-Sauveur Cathedral, where centuries of architectural styles, from the 5th to the 17th, come together in one remarkable landmark.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Independent Explorations:</strong> Enjoy free time to browse local markets and boutiques, relax at a sidewalk café or wander Aix’s delightful Provençal streets. &nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Guided walking tour of Aix-en-Provence.</li>\n\t<li>A visit to the Cours Mirabeau.</li>\n\t<li>A visit to the Mazarin Quarter.</li>\n\t<li>A visit to Saint-Sauveur Cathedral.</li>\n\t<li>Free time for independent exploration.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/820043-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDcyNTd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0ZpTDJobE5pODVOakUzTWpBMU16STVPVFV3THpneU1EQTBNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w1OGUxNDFkMWY2NDRhZjg0OWZjY2NkZDFkYTM0ZGJiNTIxYmJhNzc1YWI5YWE1ZWZmNDBkOGIxNzA4ZjljZWEx', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '820053', 'port_slug': 'marseilles-provence', 'title': 'Aix en Provence, Cheese and Wine', 'slug': 'aix-en-provence-cheese-and-wine-820053', 'price': 129.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 4.5, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': 'Leaving the harbor of Marseille, you will drive to the charming old town of Aix. This was capital of the Provence region and its attractions are numerous. First you will embark on a walking tour of the Cours Mirabeau. The wide avenue is shaded by trees and was built in the 1600s on the site of the city&rsquo;s medieval ramparts; its verdant tunnel of foliage protects pedestrians from the heat of the Provencal sun. The aristocratic facades of the old mansions line the Cours and their wrought-iron balconies and finely carved doorways invite visitors to explore. <p><br /> </p> <p>You will see a fountain dating back to 1743, particularly noteworthy for producing 93oF water which the Romans believed had healing properties. Note the different architectural styles of Saint Sauveur Cathedral with a Romanesque nave, a Merovingian baptistery and a Gothic section. These various styles date between the 5th and 17th centuries. Whatever your interest, the ambiance of Aix-en Provence makes for an enjoyable excursion in France.</p> <p>Your guide will then lead you to a cheese shop with a restaurant above in a typical Provencal street. You&rsquo;ll enjoy a wine &amp; cheese tasting, both are cleverly matched to let you savor these French delicacies. Before re-boarding your coach, you will enjoy some free time in the city and then return back to the ship. The tasting consists of a variety of 6 different cheeses &amp; 3 types of wine.&nbsp;</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Aix-en-Provence-Cheese-and-Wine-20HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3w0NjQ2OTJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaG1OaTlvTkRndk9EZ3hOREl6TkRFM016UTNNQzVxY0djfDFkYWQ3MDBjOTJlOWY1ZWM3YWZkMTgwNjAwYTNhZGE0MzI0NzhmNGYzNWViMmU1MWRkZDNjNDA5Yjk2MmU2ODc', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '820050', 'port_slug': 'marseilles-provence', 'title': "Avignon, Pope's Palace & Pont Du Gard", 'slug': 'avignon-pope-s-palace--pont-du-gard-820050', 'price': 139.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.5, 'review_count': 4, 'desc_html': '<p>Travel for approximately 1.5 hours to the breath-taking Pont du Gard, a world famous ancient Roman aqueduct bridge that crosses the shallow Gard River. This amazing feat of engineering used to carry around 44 million gallons of water a day. Built around the year 40 A.D., it features three impressive levels of arcades that are recessed one on top of the other reaching a height of 160 feet.&nbsp;</p> <p><span style="font-weight: lighter;">Here you will be able to absorb the magnificence of this unique 18th-century structure from a nearby vantage point. You will then drive to nearby Avignon for a walk around this historic town, with cobbled streets and narrow stairs. The town itself is still delightfully contained within its 14th-century walls and features beautifully preserved ramparts and pretty bell towers. Visit the largest Gothic construction in the world known as Palace of the Popes, home to nine Popes during the Great Schism that lasted from 1309 to 1378. A truly magnificent building you will be able to wander through the vast galleries and great halls.</span></p> <p>Enjoy some free time to have lunch on your own. Most of Avignon\'s medieval city streets are closed to vehicle traffic and are lined with boutiques and art galleries, along with craft, jewelry and souvenir shops. Return to Marseille via the highway, traveling through breath-taking countryside, which features vineyards, orchards and cypress trees.&nbsp;</p> <p><br /> </p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Avignon-Popes-Palaca-Pont-du-Gard-13HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3w0NDYwNTh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzJOQzlvTmpFdk9EZ3hOREl6TXpFNU1EUXpNQzVxY0djfGExYjkwYjViODI5N2Y4ZGVmN2EzNWFlYmIxNTUyNTI3NTM2MTg1OTVhODdmZDRmYzY5NjI4MzQzYmVkMTBkODI', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '820038', 'port_slug': 'marseilles-provence', 'title': 'Provençal Treasures: Arles & St. Remy', 'slug': 'proven-al-treasures-arles--st-remy-820038', 'price': 159.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.3, 'review_count': 4, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Artistic Arles:</strong> Explore historic Arles, one of Provence’s most captivating towns, known for remarkably preserved Roman monuments and charming streets that inspired generations of artists.&nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Local Landmarks:</strong> Admire the Roman Amphitheater and Saint-Trophime Church, two iconic Arles landmarks showcasing centuries of Roman and medieval heritage.&nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Van Gogh:</strong> Trace Van Gogh’s path through the town whose scenery inspired many of his most famous paintings and artistic achievements.&nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>French Flavors:</strong> Savor a three-course French lunch featuring regional Provençal flavors, served with your choice of wine or soft drink and coffee.&nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Provençal Charm:</strong> Enjoy a guided village walk through Saint-Rémy-de-Provence, one of Provence’s most charming villages, known for its elegant streets, welcoming atmosphere and connection to Nostradamus.&nbsp;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Independent Explorations:</strong> Take some time to venture on your own, from charming boutiques and local shops to inviting cafés.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Guided visit of Arles.</li>\n\t<li>Entrance to the Roman Amphitheater.</li>\n\t<li>Visit to Saint-Trophime Church.&nbsp;</li>\n\t<li>Three-course French lunch in a local restaurant.</li>\n\t<li>Guided walking tour of Saint-Rémy-de-Provence.</li>\n\t<li>Free time in both Arles and Saint-Rémy.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/820038-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQyNzJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREV5TDJoaFl5ODVOakUzTWpBeE9USXlNRGM0THpneU1EQXpPQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w3ZDM2ZjlmMmQ0NjNmMWQ1NWJmZTY1NTdiYWJhMGVhZGI0MDRmZGNmZTVhMmExMDY0Y2JmMTk3NTZjMmVjZDMz', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '820046', 'port_slug': 'marseilles-provence', 'title': 'Easy Tour of Marseilles & Free Time', 'slug': 'easy-tour-of-marseilles--free-time-820046', 'price': 89.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.2, 'review_count': 5, 'desc_html': '<p>Relax on a scenic ride along the famous coastal road, the Corniche J. F. Kennedy, enjoying also some photo stops within the narrated drive through the city of Marseille. Your motor coach will take you through the Old Port &quot;Le Vieux Port&quot;, where the Greeks landed in 600 BC. Continue along the beautiful coastal Corniche J.F Kennedy, which offers lovely views of offshore islands. Back in the center of Marseille, take some photos from the motor coach of Notre Dame de la Garde Basilica, the most magnificent building of its kind in southern France, with the statue of the Virgin on the top of the bell tower.</p> <p><br /> The basilica was built in the mid-1800s in a Romano- Byzantine style. Continue past the Longchamp Palace to see the historic buildings inaugurated in 1869, commemorating the arrival of water in a canal between the river Durance and Marseille. Stop at the Old Port for some free time to shop.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-ADD-Cours-dEstienne-dOrves.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyMTQyMzd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGlaaTlvTm1Ndk9EZ3hOREl6TWpNd05UWTVOQzVxY0djfDU0MjlmNjRmOTQ0Yzc3ZjA5ZmQzOGI3ODZlZTVmMmI4MWI3MjI5MzM2MWMzYmQ0ZTg0YTdhMTRiNTI1YTFkOTA', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '820051', 'port_slug': 'marseilles-provence', 'title': 'The Best of Marseilles', 'slug': 'the-best-of-marseilles-820051', 'price': 109.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 1.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': "This excursion will take you on a journey through the top ten highlights of Marseille. After a short drive from the large industrial harbor area, you will arrive in the city center and begin your sightseeing tour. First you'll pass by the magnificent Cathedral de la Major and continue along the esplanade where the new Museum of Civilizations from Europe and the Mediterranean (MuCEM) faces the sea. You'll also admire the St John Fortress and the St Laurence church. Then you'll drive to the beginning of the Old Port.&nbsp; <p><br /> </p> <p>The guide will explain details about the old center of the town, including the city hall and the historic General Hospital. Opposite the harbor you'll discover the Palace of the Pharo at the very end of the port and the late Roman style Abbey of Saint Victor. Passing through the Old Port, you'll drive up to &ldquo;Notre Dame de la Garde&rdquo; which dominates the cityscape. Pause for a photo stop and visit of the inside of the basilica. &nbsp;Continue on the scenic coastal drive along &ldquo;Corniche Kennedy Road&rdquo;. &nbsp;Admire this impressive coastline and the islands guarding Marseille&rsquo;s entrance, including the fortress of Ch&acirc;teau d'If. &nbsp;At the end of the coastal road, you'll see the beaches and pass by &ldquo;Le Chateau Borely&rdquo;, an 18th century residence in a middle of a peaceful park just a few minutes from the sea.&nbsp;</p> <p>On the way to the next stop, you will pass by the newly renovated &ldquo;Le Velodrome&rdquo; the symbolic stadium of the city. &nbsp;Finally arrive at &ldquo;Longchamp Palace&rdquo;, a monument adorned with magnificent fountains, waterfalls and gardens celebrating the arrival of water from the Durance canal in Marseille. Stop here for photos, and then rejoin the coach driving back to the Old Port, where you'll have free time to enjoy the city, before returning to the ship.&nbsp;</p> <p><br /> </p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Marseille-Shopping-33HERO.JPG?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3w1OTUwNjF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3dPQzlvTWpBdk9EZ3hOREl6TXpjNE1ESTFOQzVxY0djfGUxZGQ4NDZjOTQxMTRiNmQ3MmU1ZDhkM2IxYzQ0ZjhiYmQ3MzJiNzJlMDMxMzA0OWM1MWVhMjgyYzg3Zjg2M2M', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
