    {'code': '732009', 'port_slug': 'osaka-kyoto', 'title': 'Kyoto On Your Own', 'slug': 'kyoto-on-your-own-732009', 'price': 89.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/732009-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDU5MjV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREF6TDJnd1pTODVOVEU1TVRZME1qa3pNVFV3THpjek1qQXdPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xjMjA5ZjRmODg3OWQ3ZTVhY2EyNDAyN2MwNTI3NmQ4MzUzMDE0YzAyNzAwYmM3MTk5YzNmM2EyMzI2MzZjOTkz', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '732010', 'port_slug': 'osaka-kyoto', 'title': 'Highlights of Osaka', 'slug': 'highlights-of-osaka-732010', 'price': 109.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Osaka Castle:</strong> Embark on a scenic drive to Osaka Castle, constructed in 1583 on a raised platform to protect the ruler from sword-wielding samurai. Explore the vast 400-acre grounds and enjoy panoramic views from the observation deck, then visit the beautiful garden known for cherry trees and the museum with artifacts from 1570 to 1600.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Sumiyoshi Shrine:</strong> Visit the ancient Sumiyoshi Shrine, founded in the 3rd century and recognized as one of Japan's oldest shrines. Its unique Sumiyoshi-zukuri architecture exemplifies a traditional Japanese style without any influence from the mainland.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/732010-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDIwMzB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1prTDJnMk15ODVOVEU1TVRZek9ETTBNems0THpjek1qQXhNQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xlNjFhOGNjNTQ4NmNhNTU3MDdhMDgyM2MwNGQ0OWQ0MDAzMGU2YjM3YTdhYTA1YmMzODY4ZWNkNTc3MDU5ZmNl', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '732011', 'port_slug': 'osaka-kyoto', 'title': 'Kobe: Sake Brewery Museum & Mt. Rokko', 'slug': 'kobe-sake-brewery-museum--mt-rokko-732011', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/732011-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDUxODB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRE0wTDJnM01TODVOVEU1TVRZek5EY3pPVFV3THpjek1qQXhNUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wyNzBkMTg2ZDU5NDA4MGJkZTQyNTdiN2I5MTBlMGFiYjg2ZTlmZDU5ZWMxZTkzMTQ0YzYwNDdmYjFmMDM3Mjhj', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '732002', 'port_slug': 'osaka-kyoto', 'title': 'Kyoto: Fushimi-inari Taisha & Temples', 'slug': 'kyoto-fushimi-inari-taisha--temples-732002', 'price': 159.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/732002-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNTczNjN8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR000TDJoa05TODVOVEU1TVRZMk56RTNPVGd5THpjek1qQXdNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3wxNDBkMzkwYjQ2OTllOGEwNzI2ODBhMWE2Y2JlMGEyM2MxZDlhNzgxYjExMTQyMjZkNDEwYTEwYzgyMzExMGM4', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '732003', 'port_slug': 'osaka-kyoto', 'title': 'Kyoto: Zen & Nature', 'slug': 'kyoto-zen--nature-732003', 'price': 149.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/723003-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyODY5ODV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGt5TDJoak9DODVOVEU1TVRZMk16VTNOVE0wTHpjeU16QXdNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xiMGM2YzUzYjhmOTI2ZjA1YWMxYWVjNGQ4Y2ZmZDMxMjNiY2UzN2FiZjg1NzE2OTYyM2ZkOGYzYTE0YmUwYjQ2', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '732001', 'port_slug': 'osaka-kyoto', 'title': 'Best of Kyoto', 'slug': 'best-of-kyoto-732001', 'price': 199.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Countryside Highlights:</strong> Experience a narrated, countryside journey from Osaka to Kyoto, highlighting the stunning Toji Temple, Japan's tallest wooden pagoda, alongside the magnificent Kyoto Tower, which stands as the tallest modern structure in the city.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Historic Kyoto &amp; Shopping:</strong> Explore the historic Nijo Castle, completed in 1603, and marvel at its Ninomaru Palace with its unique nightingale floors. Visit the stunning 14th-century Golden Pavilion adorned with gold leaf before enjoying a Western-style lunch at a local hotel. Conclude your tour at the Heian Shrine and indulge in shopping at the Kyoto Handicraft Center.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/732001-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDU5MjV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFZoTDJoa1pDODVOVEU1TVRZMk9UZ3dNVEkyTHpjek1qQXdNUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xiZDY4NzZkMWM1MzQwNTAzYzNhNmU1OTBkN2E4ZjFkNmNiNDI4ZDY1NzVlZGI3MTFkNTdkZThmM2E5NDE2YzQ1', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '732006', 'port_slug': 'osaka-kyoto', 'title': 'Nara & Osaka Castle', 'slug': 'nara--osaka-castle-732006', 'price': 149.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Todaiji Temple:</strong> Take an hour-long journey to Nara, Japan's first permanent capital, where you will see the renowned Todaiji Temple built in the year 728. Marvel at the Great Buddha Hall housing a stunning bronze Buddha and keep an eye out for Sika deer that roam the grounds of this UNESCO World Heritage Site.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Kasuga Taisha Shrine:</strong> Make your way by foot to Kasuga Taisha Shrine, celebrated as one of Nara's most beautiful Shinto shrines. Enjoy the sight of over 2,000 stone and bronze lanterns that grace the shrine's pathways.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Osaka Castle:</strong> Pause for lunch at a local restaurant and then journey to Osaka. Visit the impressive Osaka Castle, recognized for its gold and white architecture and substantial collection of historical artifacts. Experience sweeping views from the observation deck.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Dotonbori District:</strong> Witness the vibrant energy of Dotonbori District, a must-see commercial hub in Osaka with an array of shops and dining options.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/732006-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNzc3MzB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR05pTDJnMk5TODVOVEU1TVRZMU5UY3hNVEF5THpjek1qQXdOaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3wxMjAzZjQ4ZjE0N2M5MTRlZTljNmRjNTUwNWQ0MzI2NGZkMDMxNDQxZTFiNzY0ZTFhOTE2ZTU1Y2FiZGQ3ZGUy', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '716003', 'port_slug': 'otaru-sapporo', 'title': 'Jozankei Onsen', 'slug': 'jozankei-onsen-716003', 'price': 209.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/716003-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTgyNzV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFJrTDJnMk1pODVNRE0yTmpNME16a3dOVFU0THpjeE5qQXdNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3wwZWU2YWI4MjkyMzdkM2ZkNzk0ZWQ0YjcwYTViNjA3NTIyYjY2YWIwNWM0YjQ3NzBjMDdhZWFlZTFmMWVjYzAx', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '716005', 'port_slug': 'otaru-sapporo', 'title': 'Highlights of Otaru', 'slug': 'highlights-of-otaru-716005', 'price': 159.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Otaru Cultural Heritage:</strong> Explore Otaru's cultural heritage on a scenic motorcoach tour. Begin your day with a visit to the former Aoyama Villa also called the Nishin Goten (Herring Mansion). These lavish two-story wooden structures date back to the herring fishing boom of the Meiji and Taisho eras (1868-1926). Admire their lacquered floors, whitewashed walls, zelkova corridors, and intricately adorned sliding doors, featuring works by renowned painters and calligraphers of that time.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Otaru Tenguyama Ropeway:</strong> Next, head to the Otaru Tenguyama Ropeway, just 15 minutes from downtown. A 30-person gondola whisks you from the mountaintop to the mountain foot in four minutes. Admire the miniature city view and panoramic vistas of Otaru Port, Ishikari Bay, and, on clear days, Mt. Shokanbetsu and the Shakotan Peninsula.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Otaru Canal:</strong>Continue your exploration at the Otaru Canal and Shopping District, symbolizing Otaru City's history. This historic mile-long canal offers a nostalgic glimpse of the past and unique shopping and dining experiences, with preserved store warehouses from the Meiji Period (1868-1912).</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/716005-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDI2MzJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFkyTDJnd05TODRPVGt5TnpVek1UVTJNVEkyTHpjeE5qQXdOUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w5NjgwM2NiODdmMjkwNGYwMTUyNDRkODBmMDA3YTA2ZDRkNTFjMzIyZTAwYmJmMTQ2YWQ3MDBiZTA3NDc5MDQx', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '716001', 'port_slug': 'otaru-sapporo', 'title': 'Best of Otaru', 'slug': 'best-of-otaru-716001', 'price': 229.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Shin-Nantaru Market:</strong> Discover the cultural treasures of Otaru on this guided tour, visiting the renowned Shin-Nantaru market, where you can immerse yourself in the local atmosphere and interact with the vibrant community before continuing your journey.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Sumiyoshi Shrine:</strong> Stop at the iconic Sumiyoshi Shrine, a revered Shinto shrine established in 1868.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Aoyama Villa:</strong> Witness the elegant Aoyama Villa, a beautifully preserved Herring Mansion from the 1920s, with its intricate lacquered floors and zelkova wood corridors resembling a miniature Japanese castle.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Tenguyama Ropeway:</strong> Indulge in a satisfying lunch before embarking on a scenic ride on the Otaru Tenguyama Ropeway, where a 30-person gondola whisks you from the mountaintop to the foot in just four minutes. Marvel at the breathtaking panoramic views of Otaru Port, Ishikari Bay, and on clear days, even Mt. Shokanbetsu and the Shakotan Peninsula.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Canal District:</strong> Explore the charming Canal District and enjoy one hour of free time to peruse upscale boutiques, dine at exquisite restaurants, and leisurely wander along the picturesque gaslight-lined promenade.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Authentic Japanese Lunch.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/716001-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDM4NjF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREpsTDJnMFpDODVNRFF4TVRnMk1UWXdOamN3THpjeE5qQXdNUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xmYTk3ZDAyM2Q4ZGI5MGI4Mzc0OTFmNmY5Y2IyYWY3YTY1NzBiYWI0ZGY2YWE3MWUyZDlhNGE1NTk5ODQwYTRi', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '716004', 'port_slug': 'otaru-sapporo', 'title': 'Sapporo On Your Own', 'slug': 'sapporo-on-your-own-716004', 'price': 139.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 2.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Sapporo Highlights:</strong> Depart from Otaru on a comfortable motorcoach, journeying through scenic forests and countryside. Arrive in Sapporo, known for hosting the 1972 Winter Olympics. Explore Odori Park, a central hub with gardens, shops, and the iconic Sapporo TV Tower. Climb the tower for city views (weather permitting). Discover the Sapporo Beer Museum, highlighting the city's brewing history, and enjoy a fresh draft beer. Optionally, visit the Botanic Garden, part of Hokkaido University, which includes an alpine garden and Ainu artifacts.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/716004-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTM4NzB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1V3TDJnMU5pODRPVGt5TnpVeU9Ea3pPVGd5THpjeE5qQXdOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xkYjNlZGNkNzg2ZTI2MmEyODkwNjUxYjc2MGYyYjUyMTZmMzcxN2U0NjdjZDY1N2IxMGZkYjg4ZWFiNDZiMTE4', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '716008', 'port_slug': 'otaru-sapporo', 'title': 'Highlights of Sapporo', 'slug': 'highlights-of-sapporo-716008', 'price': 149.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Hokkaido Jingu Shrine:</strong> Embark on a journey to the Hokkaido Jingu Shrine, a vast sanctuary dedicated to Emperor Meiji and known for its unique status as a shrine. Marvel at the lush nature surrounding the shrine, and if luck is on your side, catch a glimpse of the charming Ezo squirrels. Discover the rich history of Hokkaido as you learn about its renaming in the late 1800s and the enshrinement of protectors during the Hokkaido Chinzashinsai festival.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Hitsujigaoka Observation Hill:</strong> Discover the legacy of Hokkaido's founding father at Hitsujigaoka Observation Hill. Marvel at the iconic bronze statue of William Smith Clark, who came to this land to mentor the future leaders of Hokkaido. Experience the spirit of frontier exploration as you take in the panoramic views of the idyllic Hokkaido scenery and the vast Ishikari Plain, a reminder of the region's pioneering origins.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Beer Museum:</strong> Dive into the history of Sapporo Beer at the Beer Museum, Japan's oldest beer museum. Step back in time as you wander through the museum's historic halls, built during the Meiji era, and discover the origins of this beloved Hokkaido brew. Uncover the secrets of Sapporo Beer's pioneering journey through interactive panels and informative videos.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/716008-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQ0NzZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR1JtTDJnM1lpODVOVEU1TVRjeE1qY3lOek0wTHpjeE5qQXdPQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w0NDE3YTY0MWJiZjk4MjQyOWVhM2ZhZWY4OTA2NTVhMzQ1YTkzMjkwZDQ5ZWJkMjA3MDI2NmYyOTY1NTllZGVi', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '716009', 'port_slug': 'otaru-sapporo', 'title': 'Cape Kamui Scenic Walk', 'slug': 'cape-kamui-scenic-walk-716009', 'price': 194.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/716009-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMjA4MzJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0l3TDJnM055ODVNRE0yTmpNMk5UVXpNalEyTHpjeE5qQXdPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wyN2JiZGIxNmQ1OWJhMDQ2N2IzNTQ1MTM5ZmM5NTJlNGQ3Yjc0YjEyMGI1NTg0ZWU3MjcxNzZkNzZkYjMzN2Yx', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '716002', 'port_slug': 'otaru-sapporo', 'title': 'Sapporo Highlights & Odori Street On Your Own', 'slug': 'sapporo-highlights--odori-street-on-your-own-716002', 'price': 159.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Sapporo Highlights:</strong> Board a comfortable motorcoach for a scenic one-hour drive from Otaru to Sapporo, Hokkaido\'s capital city. Begin your day at Odori Park, recognized as an Important Cultural Asset, with a blend of Japanese and American architectural styles. Explore the park, known for its colorful flowerbeds, fountains, and sculptures, including "Black Slide Mantra" by sculptor Isamu Noguchi. In your free time, enjoy the park\'s vibrant atmosphere, food vendors, and the Sapporo TV Tower for city views.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Market:</strong> Visit the Sapporo outer wholesale market, a popular tourist attraction offering an authentic local lifestyle experience.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/716002-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQ4NDZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR00zTDJnMk1TODRPVGt5TnpVeU5UTXpOVE0wTHpjeE5qQXdNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xjNTk3NzBjMmJhMmM5ZGZjOWY2MWU2OWFiOGMwNzU4YmJiZjgzM2YyODVjMDA5ZjI3N2YzZjZjMTEwM2I1NTNh', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
