    {'code': '925030', 'port_slug': 'sydney', 'title': 'Debark - Tour & Transfer - Sydney Sights & Bondi', 'slug': 'debark--tour--transfer--sydney-sights--bondi-925030', 'price': 84.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/925030-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQ3Nzd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFV5TDJoa05pODVNRFl5TmpNNE5qUTVNemMwTHpreU5UQXpNQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xhMDY5OGQxNWJlZjA5OWZhYWYzNmY0NDljYzIyNTlkMDUzNTNlNTYwY2UzMDU4NWM3MDI4MzdkNDU1MTQyYzg5&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '228034', 'port_slug': 'sydney', 'title': 'A City Built on Coal and Steel', 'slug': 'a-city-built-on-coal-and-steel-228034', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>New Waterford:</strong> Step into the past in New Waterford, the 40th incorporated town in North America, where the Dominion Coal Company ignited a vibrant coal mining community.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Colliery Lands Park:</strong> Visit Colliery Lands Park, the historic location of the No. 12 &amp; No. 16 Collieries, where you\'ll find the poignant Miners Monument honoring the 307 miners who perished in local coal mines, along with flags representing the various nations that contributed to Cape Breton\'s coalfields.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Miners Museum:</strong> In Glace Bay, the Cape Breton Miners Museum invites you to delve into the rich coal mining past of the region, framed by Cape Breton Island\'s stunning coastal scenery.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Ocean Deeps Colliery:</strong> Enter the Ocean Deeps Colliery beneath the museum, where a sign instructs, "Your wife and children expect you home this evening—don’t disappoint them, be careful." Put on your pit gear and hard hat as you descend into the depths for a 30-minute tour with a retired miner, sharing daring tales, tragedies and mining techniques dating back to 1720. After your journey, explore the miners\' village and grab a beloved memento from the gift shop.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Sydney Highlights:</strong> As you head back to the ship, take in the stunning sights of Sydney\'s renowned landmarks along the way.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/228022-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDE0NzB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0pqTDJnNU9DODRPVE0xTWpZd09ERTFNemt3THpJeU9EQXlNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xlNmVlZGFhY2I4ODI1YmFhYmFiOTZmYjYzYTc5YThmZTIwMmFiZjI4MDM4ZTQ5MmUyOGVjYmYwNmE2YTkxNWFl', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '228037', 'port_slug': 'sydney', 'title': 'Mussels & Music: A Cape Breton Pub Session', 'slug': 'mussels--music-a-cape-breton-pub-session-228037', 'price': 84.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Culture &amp; Music:</strong> Experience the essence of Cape Breton\'s music in an authentic pub setting, where talented local musicians bring stories and songs to life. Celebrate the island\'s rich heritage in this unforgettable "Music Island" experience.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Sips &amp; Snacks:</strong> Enjoy a mouthwatering selection of fresh east coast mussels or pita chips and dip from one of Sydney’s renowned restaurants, complemented by a flight of locally crafted beer and cider produced just minutes away. Immerse yourself in Cape Breton’s thriving craft beverage scene.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>A bowl of fresh mussels (or pita chips and dip) per person.</li>\n\t<li>Flight of four local craft beer or cider samples (4 oz each).</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/228037-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDcxNDF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRE15TDJnME1pODVNVEEzTkRFNU5qSTNOVFV3THpJeU9EQXpOeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w0YzA5NWI2OWQ5NDNiMWVkMWJiNTRmOTZkMWY4OTQzMjFlYTk3NDY0N2MxNjQ0OGY0ODRiZTQyYzAwZjc5YjM0', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '228028', 'port_slug': 'sydney', 'title': 'Sydney City Highlights', 'slug': 'sydney-city-highlights-228028', 'price': 54.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Sydney Highlights Bus Tour:</strong> Explore the charming city of Sydney on this exclusive bus tour. Founded in 1785 by the British and incorporated as a city in 1904, Sydney boasts a rich history and vibrant culture. This tour takes you through all the city's highlights, offering a comprehensive look at its historic sites and cultural landmarks, including a drive through the Membertou community.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Whitney Pier Museum:</strong> Visit the Whitney Pier Museum, dedicated to the many nationalities that founded the region. Learn about the diverse cultural heritage that still thrives in Sydney today. Enjoy a sample of a homemade oatcake, baked from a centuries-old recipe, and experience the local warmth and charm of Sydney's people.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Charlotte Street:</strong> Before returning to the port, enjoy an optional stop on Charlotte Street for those who wish to browse the local shops independently<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Admission to Whitney Pier Museum.</li>\n\t<li>Sample tasting of oatcake, served with tea or juice.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/228014-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQyOTV8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREl4TDJnNE1DODRPVE15TURjek1EUTJNRFEyTHpJeU9EQXhOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3wzZDM1YzI3MGMxMmY0MmI2ODRjZTA4YmZhNmM0NWEyZTM1OGEyNjMwNDljMjcxNTc0ZDBkN2JjMzk2OGM1ODQ4', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '228031', 'port_slug': 'sydney', 'title': 'Discover the Two Sides of Louisbourg', 'slug': 'discover-the-two-sides-of-louisbourg-228031', 'price': 84.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 2.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/228017-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNzE3OTR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0k1TDJneVlTODRPVE15TURjM01UUXlNRFEyTHpJeU9EQXhOeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w3NzY3MmY3NDM2MzRkNjRjYTYwNjM1YzU1MTBkZWE2NWM2NzFhOWRmYzA3NGI2ZjZjMWE5NTk3MzI1MGU5ZGUz&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '228030', 'port_slug': 'sydney', 'title': 'Spirit of the Fiddle', 'slug': 'spirit-of-the-fiddle-228030', 'price': 69.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/228016-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDY5NDh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0ZrTDJoaU9TODRPVE0yTWpnek1URXhORFUwTHpJeU9EQXhOaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w5NjQ2N2U0NGViMGNlNjIwNGU1M2MzYzdhYTNmYzc1NTg1YzRmYTMxNjhmN2M2YzZjM2I1MzY5ODA2MWU1M2Fi&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '228010', 'port_slug': 'sydney', 'title': 'Old Sydney Walking Tour', 'slug': 'old-sydney-walking-tour-228010', 'price': 59.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>City Walking Tour:</strong> Explore Old Sydney, the colonial town established by Loyalists in 1785. Your guide, dressed in period costume, will lead you from the pier and through streets with historic buildings. Visit St. Patrick's Church, the oldest Catholic church, and the Jost House, the oldest home showcasing three centuries of artifacts. Hear tales of love, mayhem, and murder as you explore the oldest part of town. Pass by the old market, firehouse, and Cossit House to learn about the Cossit family. Stop at St. George's Church, Sydney's oldest building, to hear its history and connection to the Cossits. After visiting St. George's Church, you can return to the pier or explore and shop on your own.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/228010-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDIyMzB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFJoTDJneFlTODRPVE15TURjeU1UazBNRGM0THpJeU9EQXhNQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w5Yjk4OTM1MDZmMTFjNWZmYzlmZGNhMzdlY2VmMmNhMWM1NzFkMGJhMzM4OGNkNTVlMGNlMjA3MDM3Y2YzMTkw', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '952037', 'port_slug': 'tallinn', 'title': 'Enchanting Estonia', 'slug': 'enchanting-estonia-952037', 'price': 154.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Explore Estonia:</strong> This tour will give you the chance to experience the enchantment of Tallinn's Old Town: narrow streets lined with medieval merchants' houses, tall gothic church spires and plenty of charming shops and cafés. Begin with a walking tour through the cobblestone streets of the Lower Old Town, where you can almost imagine yourself mingling with medieval merchants. Take a brief stop at the famous Town Hall Square, where you will have some time to look around. Then, continue to Catherine's Passage, and browse the wares in numerous craftsmen’s workshops. From there, hop over to a nearby restaurant, where you can enjoy a glass of wine, a cup of coffee or tea, a bit of dessert and some live music.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Coffee break.</li>\n\t<li>Live music.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/952037-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNTA0MTd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREZqTDJnM1l5ODRPVEV6TkRjd016STBOelkyTHprMU1qQXpOeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3w5YzNkZTk5ZWE3YTE2ZmU4MTA1ZGRjYTdkODFmNTRlY2UyY2RhYmNhYTM4MTcyMDI3OGUyNDBmN2E3YjExOGQx', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '952035', 'port_slug': 'tallinn', 'title': 'Upper Old Town & Kadriorg Palace', 'slug': 'upper-old-town--kadriorg-palace-952035', 'price': 154.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': "<p>Experience Tallinn, Estonia’s capital city, on a narrated drive and walking tour during this exciting half-day journey. Board your motorcoach for a ride to Palace Square. In the square you will see Toompea Castle, the current home of Estonia’s parliament. Next, visit a historic Russian Orthodox Cathedral. Continue to St. Mary's Cathedral. Simply called the Dome Church by locals, St. Mary’s Cathedral is the city's oldest church. Inside you will see elaborate medieval tombs and more than 60 medieval coats of arms. Next, head to the outlook point beyond Dome Church and take in panoramic views of Tallinn's red-gabled rooftops and copper church spires. Board your motorcoach and head to Kadriorg Palace. The well-preserved palace’s main hall is one of the best examples of Baroque architecture in all Northern Europe. The palace rooms are currently used as part of the Foreign Art Museum of Estonia. After visiting the museum, enjoy the colorful gardens surrounding the palace.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/952035-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDU5NjJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhREJoTDJnMVppODRPVEV6TWpFd05qY3hNVE0wTHprMU1qQXpOUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xmYjFlYTEyZjdmYTc3MTJkMzU3ZTkyMjg3NDU3MjM4OTRmMThiMDNmNDZmYTcwZTE4ZGUyYTUzYTZkY2Y2YjQz', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '952032', 'port_slug': 'tallinn', 'title': 'Old Town Tallinn & Rakvere', 'slug': 'old-town-tallinn--rakvere-952032', 'price': 204.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Rakvere Castle:</strong> Board your motorcoach and travel country roads to 14th century Rakvere Castle, built by the warrior monks of the Livonian Order. Today, the castle is a medieval experience center complete with catapults, dungeons and live cannon. Explore the ruins of the castle and enjoy lunch in its courtyard.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Tallin:</strong> Return to Tallinn for a walking tour of Toompea Hill, named for the fortress that now houses Estonia’s parliament. See the Pikk Hermann, a medieval tower some 150 ft. in height. Stroll to Palace Square, site of the Orthodox Alexander Nevsky Cathedral. Step inside to view its icons. Continue to the Dome Church, St. Mary’s Cathedral, and Tallinn's oldest church; nobility have been buried here since the 15th century. View the stone sarcophagi before enjoying free time to shop for souvenirs.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Lunch and vodka shot.</li>\n\t<li>Entrance to Rakvere castle.</li>\n\t<li>Entrance to Dome church.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/952032-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDE4ODB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRFZqTDJnMU5TODRPVEV6TWpBMU9UZzFNekV3THprMU1qQXpNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3wyNDI2NDc0ZjBmODI2OTMxOTBkNTQ2ZTFjMDRiYWQ2ZWNjODY5YTIwZGEzN2MwNmJkMTE1ZjQ5NTFlMzQ5YTY0', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '952031', 'port_slug': 'tallinn', 'title': 'A Discovery Exclusive - Ultimate Tallinn', 'slug': 'a-discovery-exclusive--ultimate-tallinn-952031', 'price': 224.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Guided Tour:</strong> Your comprehensive six-hour tour begins with a motorcoach ride to Toompea Hill. View Toompea Castle, a massive, medieval stone fortress that houses Estonia\'s current parliament. Stroll Palace Square, grandly overseen by Alexander Nevsky Cathedral, an ornate 19th century Russian Orthodox Basilica. Nearby is also Estonia’s oldest church, Tallinn\'s beloved Dome Church, founded in 1219 by Danish conquerors. Continue to a scenic overlook for sweeping views over the spires of Tallinn’s Lower Old Town. Then, head downhill to the Town Hall Square with its Gothic Town Hall, completed in 1404 and topped with a weathervane “Old Thomas," the city\'s enduring symbol. In the Lower Old Town, visit Europe’s oldest pharmacy, ”Raeapteek“. Pause for a traditional lunch, then continue to the Rotermann Quarter, a former industrial area, which has now found a new function.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Lunch.</li>\n\t<li>Entrance to the Town Hall Pharmacy.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/952031-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTkzODR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGsyTDJneE5DODRPVEV4T0RZeE1qRTVNelU0THprMU1qQXpNUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xhMzFhNDcwMDg5Y2NhNWRiYWVlNzdlMjNiZDJmNzViNmY1N2M5ZDM5NWY2MDE4MjJiM2I1MmU2ZDc3YTdmMWJl', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '952033', 'port_slug': 'tallinn', 'title': 'Best of Tallinn', 'slug': 'best-of-tallinn-952033', 'price': 164.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Tour of Tallin:</strong> Board your motorcoach and transfer to Toompea Hill. Stroll to Palace Square, site of the Orthodox Alexander Nevsky Cathedral, and view its icons. Continue to St. Mary's Cathedral, Tallinn's oldest church. View the sarcophagi before strolling to a scenic overlook for views of the Lower Old Town. Continue to Town Hall Square in the old Hanseatic City. You will also have a short coffee break in one of the restaurants located near Town Hall Square. Continue to the Great Guild Hall – one of the most distinguished public buildings of medieval Tallinn, which, in the past, was the most important guild for merchants and artisans. Enjoy free time shopping for Baltic glass, hats, quilts, and other crafts in St. Catherine's Passage. After that, rejoin the coach and drive back to the port.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Coffee break.</li>\n\t<li>Entrance to the Great Guild House (not available on June 23).</li>\n\t<li>Entrance to Dome church.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/952033-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDA5Nzh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0pqTDJnM05pODRPVEV6TWpBM056SXlNREUwTHprMU1qQXpNeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xjMDQxOTBkZmZmZDAxMWFhMWZmZmI5ZjlhOGJmMDgzNTViNDZlY2M5MmY2Njg4NjJjYTgzNTY4YmI4YjI4YTI5', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '952038', 'port_slug': 'tallinn', 'title': 'Footsteps in Old Tallinn', 'slug': 'footsteps-in-old-tallinn-952038', 'price': 124.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/952038-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQxNDd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGs1TDJnd01pODRPVEV6TkRjeE9UWXpNVFkyTHprMU1qQXpPQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xlODlmOWVmOWExODliNjk1Mjc1NjRlNGZhZWY2MWQ2OTUyMWM5M2U0ODViYzM1MjBhZjc5ZDQ0YmVmYzg5MDVl&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
