    {'code': '435009', 'port_slug': 'tortola', 'title': 'Tortola Marine Life Snorkel Adventure', 'slug': 'tortola-marine-life-snorkel-adventure-435009', 'price': 99.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.3, 'review_count': 9, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/435009-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMTcwMjF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0k0TDJobE1DODVNVEF5T1RRME5qWTFOak13THpRek5UQXdPUzFwYldjeExtcHdad3xlYjIwYjRjM2Q5ZmM3ZDQxYzQzMTIwZGI2ODkzNTc0Y2NjMWYyODhiMTMwNGYyNGQ4ZmVkZmQ3MjQ5YWNjMzVl&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '435022', 'port_slug': 'tortola', 'title': 'Town & Country Drive', 'slug': 'town--country-drive-435022', 'price': 63.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.7, 'review_count': 9, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/435022-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDc5Nzd8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0UxTDJobVlTODVNVEU1T1RnMU1EUXhORE00THpRek5UQXlNaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3wyNzQ2ZTA4OGYyNDM0NjU4NjZjMjZhMDQwNzU1YzQyNDRlODE0Y2FmN2VhNTI2NTMzMjUzZmZlYWRkNzgxMDI0&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '868008', 'port_slug': 'valletta', 'title': 'Hagar Qim, Blue Grotto & Marsaxlokk', 'slug': 'hagar-qim-blue-grotto--marsaxlokk-868008', 'price': 129.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 3.7, 'review_count': 7, 'desc_html': '<p>We will drive you to the southern part of the island and start with a visit of the Prehistoric Temple of Hagar Qim, which was built between 3500 and 3000 B.C. The temple, which is constructed solely of globigerina limestone, is standing high overlooking the islet of Filfla. We will then drive to the picturesque Blue Grotto where, weather permitting, we shall take a boat to the Grotto to view the magnificent underwater flora (boat fare included). We will then proceed to the fishing village of Marsaxlokk where you’ll have free time to stroll around the market. You can also admire the typical, traditional and brightly painted fishing boats “luzzu”, before your return drive to the ship.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Hagar-Qim-Blue-Grotto-Marsaxlokk-HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3w1MTYwMjh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaG1ZaTlvTUdJdk9EZ3hORFV3T0RZM01UQXdOaTVxY0djfDFkMzJjMDkxMDVkOTRmNzJjMGUwYTE4ZmMxNDE1ZDUxN2FkNmEyYzJhYThmMDMzNmIzODVmZTU0NTUwMzViMzU', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '868002', 'port_slug': 'valletta', 'title': 'Valletta: City of the Knights', 'slug': 'valletta-city-of-the-knights-868002', 'price': 79.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.7, 'review_count': 6, 'desc_html': "<p>Depart quayside in coaches for a short drive around Valletta’s bastions. Drive past Fort St. Elmo and stop for a photo while admiring Fort Manoel and Marsamxett Harbour. Upon arrival in Valletta, Malta's capital city, visit the Upper Barracca Gardens on foot for a panoramic view of Malta's natural harbors and the historic cities of Senglea, Cospicua and Vittoriosa. Then, proceed to St. John's Co-Cathedral – the Conventual’s Church of the Knights of Malta also including the famous masterpiece, The Beheading of Saint John the Baptist. Finally, walk to the Palace Armoury within the Magisterial Palace, formerly the residence of the Grand Masters of the Order. Enjoy some free time to explore on your own before your return drive to the ship.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-868002-Valletta-City-of-the-Knights-HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3w1MzI3NzZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzBOQzlvWkRBdk9EZ3hORFV3TmpRM05UVTFNQzVxY0djfDJjMGQ3OTMxMDZjMzFhMjk1OTBjZDRhNDk3NTVhYjc5ZGYxMzdkMWY4ZDM3NTAzN2ViYjNjNGEzYWVjMjYyZTM', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '868005', 'port_slug': 'valletta', 'title': 'Malta Highlights', 'slug': 'malta-highlights-868005', 'price': 169.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 6, 'desc_html': "<p>Travel via coach to Valletta and visit the Upper Barracca Gardens on foot. Enjoy a panoramic view of Malta's natural harbours and the historic cities of Senglea, Cospicua and Vittoriosa. Then proceed to St. John's Co-Cathedral, the Conventual Church of the Knights of Malta, where you will also see the famous masterpiece - Caravaggio's Beheading of St. John. You will then walk to MUZA – Malta’s Museum of Fine Arts. You will then be driven to Tarxien to visit the Three Neolithic Temples which are unique in the world. Enroute you will stop for lunch at Ta Maria, one of Malta’s award winning restaurants specializing in local cuisine. This stop will be followed with a visit to Malta’s Old Capital, Mdina, the Silent City. Here you will visit the Cathedral of St. Paul where Pope John Paul II chose the chapel within the cathedral to pray alone. Onto the Ramparts, dating back to the 9th century. Enjoy the scenic drive to the Glass Blowing factory, to watch local artisans at their creative work, prior to driving back to your ship.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Malta-Highlights-HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNDc1Mzh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaGpaUzlvTVRFdk9EZ3hORFV3TnpjMU16VXdNaTVxY0djfDQxZTM2NTc5ZDlmNjlhMGEzNDdhNjM5NDZkODMzNzcxODU1NTBlMjgzZTgyMjM1M2VjZjM0NTM3NWUyMmQ2ZjE', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '868013', 'port_slug': 'valletta', 'title': 'Top 10 Best of Malta', 'slug': 'top-10-best-of-malta-868013', 'price': 129.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': '<p>You will depart quay accompanied by a guide and enjoy an entire day admiring the top best 10 sites which the island of Malta can offer. Your first stop is Valletta, the fortress city named after its founder Jean Parisot de La Vallette. Your guide will stop in front of Auberge de Castille, one of the finest architectures of Malta which today houses the office of the Prime Minister. Walk to the Upper Barracca Gardens which offer amazing views of the Grand Harbour and the Three Cities. A visit to St. John’s Co-Cathedral cannot be missed. It is Malta’s greatest treasure including the famous painting by Caravaggio – The Beheading of Saint John the Baptist. Take your coach and drive to Vittoriosa, one of the three cities which rightly claims to be the cradle of Maltese history. Continue to Marsaxlokk for a photo stop of a typical fishing village, where one can admire colorful fishing boats known by the Maltese as ‘luzzu’. Drive past Buskett, which is the only woodland area in Malta planted by the Knights of St. John.<br />\n<br />\nProceed to Rabat where you will mingle with the locals at a typical local meeting spot and taste Maltese delicacies which the Maltese are so proud of. Walk to Mdina, Malta’s old capital which also happens to be the location used in a popular film and T.V. series. Enjoy free time to wander around the narrow streets of the town. Then you’ll be driven via Mosta, famous for its Dome, on your return to the ship.</p>', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Top-10-Best-of-Malta-HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyNzk5NDF8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyaG1aaTlvWldFdk9EZ3hORFV3T1RVMU5UYzBNaTVxY0djfGU3NDFhZGUxNTU0YTU3ODZjZWM4ZmU0M2E2ODYzOTVlYzkyYmQwZmI4NzVlYzAyY2IwNzViOTAzOTIzYTg3MzE', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '868010', 'port_slug': 'valletta', 'title': 'Malta’s Noble Heritage', 'slug': 'malta-s-noble-heritage-868010', 'price': 89.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': "<strong>Palazzo Parisio & Gardens:</strong> Travel with your guide to Naxxar for a visit to Palazzo Parisio, a 19th-century palace that reflects the lifestyle and ambitions of a Maltese noble family. Explore its elegant interiors and stroll through two baroque walled gardens, including the historic orangerie, while learning about the palace's place in Malta's heritage.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>San Anton Gardens:</strong> Continue to San Anton Gardens, created by Grand Master Antoine de Paule as the grounds of his summer residence, San Anton Palace. Today, the palace serves as the residence of the Maltese President. Walk among mature trees, stone urns, fountains, ponds and formal flower beds, and see plaques commemorating ceremonial tree plantings by visiting heads of state. The gardens are also home to a variety of plants, including jacaranda trees, Norfolk pines, bougainvillea and roses.\n<br /><br />\n<strong>Casa Rocca Piccola:</strong> Drive to Valletta, Malta's capital city, and visit Casa Rocca Piccola, home of the 9th Marquis and Marchioness de Piro. Meet the current owners and discover the customs and traditions of Maltese nobility through 400 years of family history. During your visit, view collections of furniture, silver and paintings that offer insight into Malta's cultural heritage.", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-Maltas-Noble-Heritage-HERO.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3w0NDAwMzZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzROeTlvTVdZdk9EZ3hORFV3T1RBNU5qazVNQzVxY0djfDliZjI1MjhkYjBlMWU5NjE5NDcyYmZkYzRmODI0NzRmZGUyYmYyMjAxOGNjMTIxN2Q3MzJlNWNmMzFhZWVhM2E', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
