    {'code': '819044', 'port_slug': 'warnemunde-berlin', 'title': 'Berlin by train:Berlin & Sachsenhausen Camp(Lunch)', 'slug': 'berlin-by-train-berlin--sachsenhausen-camp-lunch-819044', 'price': 479.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 5.0, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/819044-img2.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDQ1MzB8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGhrTDJneVl5ODRPVEkxTVRRek16TTBPVFF5THpneE9UQTBOQzFwYldjeUxtcHdad3xhN2UzODVjNjQyMjY2N2RlY2Y5MmQ0MmU5NTEzZjExM2UyMzkyMWM0YjNlYWQwM2ZkYzZlMjBkYWYzMmZhNTUz&w=700&h=550&resize_profile=pdpgallery', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '819046', 'port_slug': 'warnemunde-berlin', 'title': 'Berlin by Train: Berlin On Your Own', 'slug': 'berlin-by-train-berlin-on-your-own-819046', 'price': 279.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 1.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': None, 'image_url': 'https://www.carnival.com/shop/medias/819046-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDgwOTZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRE5pTDJnNVpDODRPVEkxTVRRMU1EY3hOalEyTHpneE9UQTBOaTFwYldjeExtcHdad3wxNzZhYjYzNTdlMGFhODY5NjU4MmQ0YTEwZDE5ZTA0NTliZDA5MmQ0MzAzOGRkMjRhMjUxMTVkZDgwNmNmNGZj&w=1232&h=647&resize_profile=pdphero', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '819040', 'port_slug': 'warnemunde-berlin', 'title': "Rostock's Top 10 by Road, River & Rail", 'slug': 'rostock-s-top-10-by-road-river--rail-819040', 'price': 219.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.5, 'review_count': 2, 'desc_html': '<p><strong>Travel Like a Local:</strong> Experience Rostock like a local, with a scenic coach transfer and a public tram ride into the historic city center.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Rostock Stroll:</strong> Explore Rostock’s historic heart on a guided walking tour, where you’ll discover Mecklenburg-Vorpommern’s largest city, its Hanseatic history, vibrant shopping streets, and remarkable post-war restoration.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Local Treasures:</strong> Uncover Rostock’s historic and architectural highlights, including the exterior of the University of Rostock, Northern Europe’s oldest university, the Gothic Town Hall, and St. Mary’s Church.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Independent Explorations:</strong> Take leisure time to shop on pedestrian-friendly streets or visit St. Mary’s Church independently to further discover this historic site.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Sip &amp; Sail:</strong> Relax on a Warnow River cruise back to Warnemünde and enjoy traditional German beer or sparkling wine along the way.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Public tram ride into Rostock city center.</li>\n\t<li>Guided walking tour.</li>\n\t<li>Warnow River boat cruise.</li>\n\t<li>Traditional German beer or sparkling wine.</li>\n</ul>\n', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/819040-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDAyMzR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0U0TDJnM01DODRPVEkxTVRRM09UVTFNak13THpneE9UQTBNQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w4Zjc1MzUxMjBiZmJlZDU0ZDY5Zjk5NWYzOTMxMzA1YzJlZTFhOTc5OWNkZTVhZjZjM2VlNjRjMDI0YTg1MWNh', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '857006', 'port_slug': 'zeebrugge-brussels', 'title': 'Bruges & Beer Tasting', 'slug': 'bruges--beer-tasting-857006', 'price': 149.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': 'This half-day adventure in Bruges Old Town will take you past timeless medieval architecture and prominent landmarks before taking you to a local beer tasting. Your tour begins when you arrive in Bruges Old Town. There, you’ll follow your guide to the 775-year-old Belfry of Bruges, a medieval bell tower and one of the city’s most prominent landmarks. Nearby is the Town Hall, built between 1376 and 1420, and one of the oldest guild halls in the Low Countries of Europe. Then, have your camera ready for one of the square’s most notable sights, the Basilica of the Holy Blood. Originally built in the 12th century to hold a holy relic, this Romanesque-style church is known for its gleaming, sculpted statues and stunning 18th-century stained glass windows (exterior viewing only). After sightseeing, your guide will take you to a delightful local café for a beer tasting. Finally, explore on your own for approximately 30 minutes before rejoining your motor coach and heading back to port.', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-bruges-and-belgian-beer-tasting-857006-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTg5ODJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZ3lNQzlvTURFdk9EZ3lNelE1TlRrMU1ETTJOaTVxY0djfDZiNTdlNDFmYjllZTkxOWU3NTFkNDJlYmI4NTgyODNjYjgyODY4MjIzNDYxZjg0ZjNlMjQyODU2YTA0MDJkOTA', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '857014', 'port_slug': 'zeebrugge-brussels', 'title': 'Bruges & Canal Cruise', 'slug': 'bruges--canal-cruise-857014', 'price': 204.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 4.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': 'Once you arrive in Bruges, your guided half-day tour begins with a walk along the cobbled streets and around the historic Market Square, which is home to the historical guild halls and many other centuries-old buildings. Stroll past the Belfry, a huge bell tower that houses 48 bells, plus the impressive Town Hall and the 12th-century Basilica of the Holy Blood. Then, enjoy a scenic cruise around the city’s charming canals, which boast views of medieval and Renaissance buildings, many of which sit directly on the water. This intimate approach to the sights makes the cruise a great way to discover this amazing city. Afterward, take advantage of a photo stop at the 13th-century Church of Our Lady, home to Michelangelo’s white marble sculpture, Madonna and Child (exterior viewing only). Then, head to the Walplein and enjoy some free time to browse the shops for fine Belgian chocolates or Flemish lace. Or you can stop by a local cafe for some coffee or locally brewed beer.', 'image_url': '/shop/medias/bruges-and-canal-cruise-857014-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDY5ODh8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzVPQzlvT1dZdk9EZ3lNVGMxTnpBMU1Ea3hNQzVxY0djfGUyOGQ3NjNjMjI4NmQ5ZTA3MzRlZWIwNDliMDk3YjlkMmI1MTVhYmNkZTdiNGQxMWYwNTAzOTYwZmVhNWZjMzQ', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '857017', 'port_slug': 'zeebrugge-brussels', 'title': 'Best of Brussels', 'slug': 'best-of-brussels-857017', 'price': 144.99, 'price_unit': 'Adult', 'rating': 2.0, 'review_count': 1, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Panoramic Drive:</strong> Relax and enjoy a scenic drive from Zeebrugge to Brussels. Upon arrival in the capital, take a panoramic drive past King Boudewijn Stadium and the Centenaire. Stop for a photo opportunity at the Atomium statue. Continuing on, you will view the Chinese Pavilion, the Japanese Tower and the Royal Castle of Laeken.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Walking Tour:</strong> At the Central Station, disembark for a guided walk through the city. Stroll through Old Town area and around the Grand Place with its Baroque guild houses and ornate Town Hall. Walk through St. Hubert Arcade with its myriad of shops, and down Butchers' Street, rich with restaurants and cafés. Walk a few more blocks to view the Manneken Pis Statue.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>What’s Included:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Guided panoramic drive.</li>\n\t<li>Guided walking tour in Brussels.</li>\n\t<li>Free time for shopping.</li>\n</ul>\n", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/857017-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDU5ODZ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhR0kzTDJnME1TODRPVGN4TVRNNU9EUXlNRGM0THpnMU56QXhOeTFwYldjeExtcHdad3xmZWIxYmY5YTI0ZGNiODc3MmMzNjA1YTE3YjVjOGVhNThlNTdkMzIwZmZjZDQ1NGI0MDE5MGNmMDliODQzZjBl', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '857024', 'port_slug': 'zeebrugge-brussels', 'title': 'Highlights of Ghent by Canal Cruise', 'slug': 'highlights-of-ghent-by-canal-cruise-857024', 'price': 159.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': 4.7, 'review_count': 3, 'desc_html': "<p><strong>Panoramic Tour:</strong> Begin your half-day adventure with a scenic ride through the Flemish countryside to Ghent, a medieval town full of history.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Canal Cruise:</strong> Board a canal boat for a comprehensive tour of the city's past and present, gliding past historic guildhalls, the impressive Castle of the Counts, and ancient markets.<br />\n<br />\n<strong>Ghent on Foot:</strong> Wander through Ghent's narrow, pedestrian-friendly streets. Discover unique architecture, stylish bars, charming waffle houses, and shops filled with fine chocolates and Flemish lace. Your tour will conclude with a short boat transfer back to your coach.</p>", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/857024-img1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wzMDU3OTR8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhRGN5TDJnek1pODVNREl5TVRVek1EazNNalEyTHpnMU56QXlOQzFwYldjeExtcHdad3w1MDI1OWRkOWE5YWUyMjk4ZjAzZjhjNDlmMzdjNDA2ZTNmZmY4M2Q1MmYwMTliZTE5ZTIxYjAwOGY2YjcxNGM4', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
    {'code': '857013', 'port_slug': 'zeebrugge-brussels', 'title': 'Flemish Countryside', 'slug': 'flemish-countryside-857013', 'price': 114.99, 'price_unit': 'Person', 'rating': None, 'review_count': 0, 'desc_html': "During the 4-hour tour, you’ll have ample time to explore the quaint, medieval town of Damme on your own and at your own pace. You’ll begin at Market Square, the site of the charming Town Hall. Originally constructed in 1241, the building boasts a tower with 25 bells and a timepiece from 1459, believed to be Belgium’s oldest. The quiet beauty of Our Ladies Church, built in 1225, is one of Damme’s most renowned monuments. Another of Damme’s ancient buildings is Saint-John's Hospital. Founded in 1249 to care for the poor, the chapel and infirmary are still in their original condition. Continue south of Bruges, to the peaceful village of Loppem, where one of the main attractions is undoubtedly the stunning castle. <br><br> Loppem Castle has a particular and homogenous style, in the sense that the architecture and the interior have retained their original state. It was in 1856 that the future castellans, Baron Charles van Caloen and his wife, Countess Savina de Gourcy Serainchamps, appointed the English architect Edward Welby Pugin (whose father, August Welby Northmore Pugin, participated in the building of the Westminster Houses of Parliament) with the task of designing the plans for the castle. Pugin's task was pursued by Jean Bethune, who brought a more Flemish character to the construction. Loppem Castle later came to play a prominent role in the political history of Belgium at the end of World War I. Stroll along the landscaped walkways that wind through the trees and across bridges. You’ll get a chance to buy some Belgian chocolates at one of the largest chocolate shops in the region before returning to port.", 'image_url': '/shop/medias/y01-flemish-countryside-857013-1.jpg?context=bWFzdGVyfGltYWdlc3wyOTkxMjJ8aW1hZ2UvanBlZ3xhVzFoWjJWekwyZzBZeTlvTVRVdk9EZ3lNelE1Tmpnek5URXdNaTVxY0djfGNhYWRkZDYyNmZlYmQ0M2QwZWFiODFiMzU2MTZjMjhiZWRkNjRiMzViM2U5ZDIyMTk0ZmEzNjA4YzEwZGM0MGE', 'duration': '', 'activity_level': '', 'min_age': ''},
